2026-08-16 11:02:46,238 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'park-automation-module', 'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'PETER\'S WORDS, VERBATIM (2026-08-14):\n\n"automation. I need an automation module, this would mostly involve things like what I did 30 minutes ago, a remote survey where I pinged home 11 times to test different antannae locations. an example would be a verb command such as point xxx - point the yagi at me, ping xxxx ping would reply with pong and would provide info about rssi / snr / hops and sig quality. route xxx would do a tracerout to me. I have not thought of all of the things I need yet, those are just examples: verb arg notes somthing like that, but that is just a starting point and not a full final spec, you probably have other suggestions. ?"\n\nEXPLICITLY NOT A FINAL SPEC. He says so himself, twice, and asks for suggestions.\nDo not treat the three verbs as the requirement list.\n\nTHE DRIVING USE CASE, IN HIS WORDS: a REMOTE SURVEY. He was away from home,\npinged home 11 times, moving the antenna between pings to compare locations. So\nthe module\'s job is to let ONE PERSON IN THE FIELD drive the home station and\nget a measurement back, without a second operator at the dashboard.\n\nSTARTING VERBS HE NAMED:\n  point <node>   aim the YAGI at me\n  ping  <node>   reply pong, carrying rssi / snr / hops / signal quality\n  route <node>   traceroute to me\n\nOPEN QUESTIONS TO PUT TO HIM WHEN THIS IS PICKED UP (not answered here):\n  - where is the verb TYPED? a mesh text message from his handheld, a dashboard\n    page, or both? The remote-survey use case implies over the mesh, which makes\n    this a receive-and-act path node-dash does not have today.\n  - a survey is a SEQUENCE, not one verb. Does he want a recorded run — 11 pings,\n    each stamped with what the antenna was doing — so the comparison is a table\n    rather than his memory? That is the actual deliverable behind "I pinged home\n    11 times".\n  - NEVER SEND ON PRIMARY. Any verb that transmits must be Private-channel or a\n    DM to his own nodes.\n  - the rotator is SHARED (the garage alarm uses it too). `point` must\n    point-and-hold briefly then release, never take a long lockout.\n\nRELATED EXISTING WORK, to read before designing anything: docs/modules/rotator.md\n(point_target / hold semantics), active-tracker.js (already emits per-packet\nrssi/snr for a targeted node), traceroute lifecycle in src/, and the mission\nrunner (src/mission-runner.js, src/probe-plan.js) which may already be half of\nthe "sequence of steps with recorded attempts" machinery.'}
