2026-08-16 11:13:08,214 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'task': 'bugs', 'title': 'GAP - our own signal_update shape is now unvalidated, because the test SKIPs it outside scan mode', 'description': 'CONFIRMED 2026-08-14, created BY the fix in commit d2f9002 and recorded rather than left implicit.\n\nBefore the fix, `tests/test_node.py` validated `signal_update` against a sample —\nand failed, because the sample it caught was mesh-gw\'s flat one. With the gw\'s now\nconsumed at the boundary, the type is absent outside scan mode, so the test reports:\n\n    [○] SKIP    WS:signal_update  — only during SCAN mode\n\nThat CONDITIONAL is now TRUE for the first time (it resolves the earlier ledger\nentry "test_node\'s CONDITIONAL says signal_update fires only during SCAN mode;\nmeasured false"). But the consequence is that OUR nested shape\n`{type, data:{signal_num, rssi, snr, ts}}` is now covered by nothing.\n\nTHIS IS A REAL WEAKENING, not bookkeeping: the check that would catch a future\nchange to the tracker\'s payload no longer runs in the ordinary case.\n\nTWO WAYS OUT, neither chosen here:\n  - drive a scan during the test so the event actually fires, and validate it\n  - assert the shape at the emit site instead of on the wire\n\nDo not "fix" this by removing the CONDITIONAL — that would make an honest SKIP\ninto a spurious FAIL on every run.'}
2026-08-16 11:13:17,207 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'signal-update-shape-collision', 'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Stop mesh-gw\'s flat `signal_update` reaching the browser, where it is silently discarded.\n\nTwo producers, one type name, incompatible shapes:\n  mesh-gw AppRouter  FLAT    {type, __ble_addr, addr, from_num, snr, rssi, hops}\n                             one per packet carrying rx_rssi/rx_snr — constantly\n  our YAGI tracker   NESTED  {type, data:{signal_num, rssi, snr, ts}}\n                             active-tracker.js, only while aimed at a node\n\npublic/app-ws.js reads ev.data, so flat ones fail the guard and return with no\nerror and no log. Measured 2026-08-14: 9 discarded in 60 s with no scan running.\n\nPeter, 2026-08-14, when told this and the wider passthrough both needed fixing:\n"you can decide on the order and whether you split it. fact is they need fixing"\n\nDELIBERATELY SCOPED TO DOMAIN 1. No public/ change. The wider defect — the\nhandler\'s final broadcast(ev) forwarding every unrecognised gw event verbatim,\nwhich is how these arrived — is its own task, because fixing it spans both\ndomains and CLAUDE.md forbids that in one task.'}
2026-08-16 11:13:21,699 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'signal-update-shape-collision', 'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Consume the gw\'s at the boundary in src/ws-relay.js, in the AppRouter translations\nblock, before any other handling:\n\n    if (ev.type === \'signal_update\' && ev.data === undefined) return;\n\nDiscriminate on the WRAPPER, not a field list, so a new field on either side never\nneeds a change here. _hintNodeStatus has already run at the top of the handler, so\nthe node-status hint still fires and nothing is lost.\n\nDo NOT wrap the gw\'s payload in `data`: from_num is the node the packet came FROM,\nsignal_num is the node the YAGI is AIMED AT. Merging mis-attributes a reading.\n\nSpec: docs/modules/ws-relay.md, new section under "Event routing".\nValidation: python scripts/check_specs.py + python3 tests/test_node.py.\nReached-not-merely-present: disable the guard with `if (false && ...)`, restart,\nre-tap, confirm the flat ones return, restore.'}
