2026-08-16 11:13:36,970 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'browser-must-not-see-raw-gw-events', 'title': 'BUG - ws-relay forwards unrecognised mesh-gw events to the browser verbatim, breaking the zero-gw-knowledge rule', 'steps': ['Investigate: enumerate every gw type crossing verbatim and every public/ consumer of each', 'DISCUSS with Peter: split into a Domain 1 task and a Domain 2 task, and agree the node-dash-owned shapes', 'Document', 'Implement', 'Observe', 'Track']}
2026-08-16 11:13:49,942 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'browser-must-not-see-raw-gw-events', 'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'CLAUDE.md, Domain 2: the browser "Consumes: node-dash backend API only. Does not\nknow that mesh-gw exists. Zero gw API knowledge."\n\n`src/ws-relay.js` breaks that. The last statement of `bridge.on(\'event\', ...)` is\n`broadcast(ev)` — a catch-all that forwards every gw event no earlier branch\nconsumed, verbatim, to the browser.\n\nPeter, 2026-08-14, on whether this was a preference: "wel that is not a matter of\npreferences that is a matter of right and wrong isnt it ?" — and then: "you can\ndecide on the order and whether you split it. fact is they need fixing"\n\nMEASURED 2026-08-14, 60 s tap on ws://127.0.0.1:8000/events compared against the\nsame window on mesh-gw\'s own ws://127.0.0.1:8001/events. Five types cross with a\nkey signature byte-identical to mesh-gw\'s:\n\n  type             frames/60s   public/ references\n  packet                   42   4      reads mesh-gw\'s raw shape\n  node_info                 9   1      reads mesh-gw\'s raw shape\n  signal_update             9   1      FIXED separately, commit d2f9002\n  private_app               2   0      NOTHING reads it — pure leak\n  message_status            1   1      reads mesh-gw\'s raw shape\n\n`__ble_addr` — mesh-gw\'s own internal identity field, added by its identity layer\n(docs/gw/modules/bridge_identity.md) — rides on four of those five. `grep\n__ble_addr public/*.js` returns NOTHING, so it is carried to the browser and never\nused.\n\nWHY THIS IS NOT JUST TIDINESS: signal_update was invisible for an unknown length of\ntime precisely because the browser was coded against a gw shape. When mesh-gw\nchanged or added a producer, the browser broke silently. Every type in that table\ncarries the same exposure.\n\nSCOPE WARNING: `packet`, `node_info` and `message_status` are READ by public/, so\ngiving them node-dash-owned shapes changes both domains. CLAUDE.md: "No fix may\nspan domains in a single task." Step 2 exists to split this before any code is\nwritten. `private_app` may be separable — nothing reads it, so ceasing to forward\nit is Domain 1 alone.'}
