2026-08-16 11:14:26,565 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'park-automation-module', 'kind': 'note', 'text': 'PETER, VERBATIM, 2026-08-14 — SECOND INSTALMENT, same subject as the goal note:\n\n"the automation needs to be designed as configurable, such that I can add new automations and select / define what it can do. I accept that might not be entirely possible without some kind of scripting, I have no idea how that would work, but there are a few which I need quickly. maybe initially they would not be 100% confiugurable but hard coded."\n\nFILED AS A NOTE ON THIS TASK, NOT A SEPARATE PARK, because it is the same idea\ngaining a requirement. Splitting it would have hidden the constraint from anyone\nreading the goal.\n\nWHAT THIS CHANGES ABOUT THE DESIGN:\n\n  - CONFIGURABILITY IS A REQUIREMENT, not a nice-to-have. He wants to add new\n    automations and define what each may do, himself, without a code change.\n  - HE HAS ALREADY CONCEDED THE HARD PART. "might not be entirely possible without\n    some kind of scripting" and "I have no idea how that would work" — so the\n    scripting/DSL question is OPEN and his, not something to quietly decide.\n  - HE HAS AUTHORISED A STAGED BUILD. "there are a few which I need quickly. maybe\n    initially they would not be 100% confiugurable but hard coded." Hard-coded\n    first is explicitly acceptable. Do NOT hold the useful ones behind a general\n    engine.\n\nTHE TRAP THIS SETS, and it is the whole reason to write it down: "hard-coded now,\nconfigurable later" only survives if the hard-coded ones are built AS INSTANCES OF\nTHE EVENTUAL MODEL — same verb table, same argument shape, same permission check —\nrather than as three bespoke handlers that later have to be thrown away. Get the\nSHAPE right even while the content is fixed.\n\n"SELECT / DEFINE WHAT IT CAN DO" IS A PERMISSION MODEL, and it is the safety-critical\nhalf. These automations TRANSMIT and MOVE HARDWARE. Whatever is built must be able to\nexpress: never on the PRIMARY channel; which nodes may be addressed; how long the\nrotator may be held (it is SHARED with the garage alarm); how often a verb may fire.\nThose constraints exist in this repo today only as prose and comments.\n\nSTILL TO ASK HIM (carried from the goal note, unanswered): where the verb is typed\n(mesh text from his handheld, or a dashboard page), and whether a survey run should\nbe RECORDED as a comparable table rather than remembered.'}
