2026-08-16 12:39:06,688 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'private-channel-resolver', 'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'New module src/channels.js — the only place that answers "which channel is this".\n\n  pskFingerprint(psk)            sha256 hex; NULL for an absent/empty key so an\n                                 unencrypted channel can never compare equal\n  privateFp()                    the configured designation, or null\n  isPrivate(device, index)       the only permitted "is this private" test\n  privateIndexFor(device)        the slot to transmit on, per radio, or NULL\n  resolveChannel(device, index)  {index, name, role, psk_fp, is_private}\n  channelsFor(device)            every known channel on that radio\n  setDeviceChannels(device, ch)  fed by ws-relay; this module does NO HTTP\n\nConfig `channels.private_psk_fp` designates which key is the private one. It\ncannot be derived — the two PRIMARYs are shared across both radios too.\n\nsrc/ws-relay.js refreshDeviceChannels() computes psk_fp and feeds the resolver, so\nthe send form and the resolver read one table and cannot disagree. The browser is\nserved `is_private` per channel and NEVER the fingerprint.\n\nFAILS SAFE: privateIndexFor returns null, never 0. A fallback to 0 is PRIMARY,\nwhich is the public mesh.\n\nSpec: docs/modules/channels.md. Validation: check_specs + a live device_list tap.\nReached-not-merely-present: delete the config row, restart, confirm every\nis_private goes false and privateIndexFor goes null; restore.'}
