2026-08-16 13:18:28,729 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'app-perf-persistset-global', 'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'app-perf.js was the only module reaching persistSet through the window global that\napp.js:26 sets for app-node-status.js. Eight other modules import it properly.\n\nCAME OUT OF DISPROVING A LEDGER ENTRY. Bugs step 74 read "app-perf.js calls\npersistSet() with no import — latent ReferenceError". The first half is true, the\nconclusion is not: window.persistSet is assigned at load, every call site is in a\nhandler body, so it always resolved. No ReferenceError has ever been possible.\n\nWhat was actually wrong is smaller and real: six call sites depending on a line in\nanother module that exists for a third module\'s benefit. Tidying app.js:26 away\nwould have broken all six, silently, at runtime only.\n\nSHIPPED 48ee64d. One import line.\n\nPROVEN REACHED IN A REAL BROWSER at 1600x1000: replaced window.persistSet with a\nfunction that throws, drove perfSetExpert() through Alpine, and\nui_prefs.perfExpert went "true" -> "false" with threw:null. The import is what\nruns. Preference restored to "true" afterwards.\n\nNO SCREENSHOT — browser_take_screenshot reported success but no file reached this\nfilesystem; the browser is not on this host. Layout was measured in-page instead\n(0 cropped .card-body, 0 off-screen .card, no horizontal overflow, charts\npresent). Proportionate for an import with no visual surface; it would not be for\na real UI change, and the screenshot path needs fixing before the next one.'}
