2026-08-16 13:21:53,354 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'task': 'bugs', 'title': 'BUG - the YAGI has completed ZERO traceroutes since 2026-08-12; 2,778 attempts, five days, a hard changepoint', 'description': 'CONFIRMED by measurement 2026-08-16, and it is the most serious thing in this\nledger. Found during an audit, not reported by anything — nothing on the dashboard\nsays the YAGI has stopped working.\n\nTHE CHANGEPOINT IS ABSOLUTE, NOT A DEGRADATION:\n\n  select date(ts,\'unixepoch\') day, count(*) attempts,\n         sum(case when status=\'ok\' then 1 else 0 end) ok\n    from traceroute_history where tx_device like \'F4%\'\n      and ts > strftime(\'%s\',\'now\')-14*86400 group by day order by day desc;\n\n  2026-08-16   335  0        2026-08-11   400  27\n  2026-08-15   594  0        2026-08-10   225  30\n  2026-08-14   678  0        2026-08-09   333  65\n  2026-08-13   645  0        2026-08-08   337  51\n  2026-08-12   526  0        2026-08-07   135  23\n                             2026-08-06   121  33\n                             ...18-65 ok every day before\n\nWorking through 2026-08-11. Exactly zero every day from 2026-08-12. 2,778\nconsecutive failures.\n\nCONTROLLED — this is NOT "the YAGI gets harder targets". Restricted to the 52\nnodes BOTH radios attempted in the last 24 h:\n\n  OMNI  E9:B0:3F:17:27:91   316 attempts   61 ok   19.3%\n  YAGI  F4:12:FA:39:F7:B6   492 attempts    0 ok    0.0%\n\nSame targets, same window, same mesh. One radio 19%, the other absolute zero.\n\nWHAT I RULED OUT, each with its own check:\n  NOT misattribution to the OMNI — if YAGI replies were being credited to the\n    OMNI, OMNI\'s successes would have JUMPED on 08-12. They fell: 123 ok on\n    08-11 -> 65 on 08-12, and its rate is roughly flat-declining throughout\n    (18.2% -> 16.4% -> 11.8%). Nothing was gained where the YAGI lost it.\n  NOT a LoRa/modem divergence — GET /<addr>/config/lora is IDENTICAL on both\n    radios: EU_868, preset, BW 250, SF11, CR5, hop_limit 7, tx_enabled true,\n    tx_power 27, rx_boosted_gain true.\n  NOT a node-dash commit — there are NO commits between 08-11 and 08-12 21:49,\n    and the whole of 08-12 (526 attempts) is already zero before those land.\n  NOT "it cannot hear" — the YAGI received and answered a live @ping and @point\n    on the private channel on 2026-08-16.\n\nWHAT I DID NOT ESTABLISH: the cause. The observation is solid and the explanation\nis not mine to invent. Candidates, untested: physical (antenna, cable, connector,\na rotator-borne feed), something specific to the transmitting-radio dispatch path\nfor the rotator radio, or an environmental//mesh-side change on 11-12 Aug.\n\nRELATED AND COMPOUNDING, not the same thing: 100% of YAGI traceroutes in the last\n24 h carried aim_mode=\'none\' across 60 distinct rotator azimuths (see the\nyagi-transmits-unaimed entry). Unaimed would DEGRADE a success rate. It does not\nexplain 492 consecutive zeros against targets the OMNI reaches — so there are\nlikely two faults here, not one.\n\nWHY IT WENT UNNOTICED FOR FIVE DAYS: nothing watches per-radio success. The\nPerformance page shows one combined rate (12%), which stays plausible because the\nOMNI carries it. A radio can go completely dead and the dashboard reads "low but\nworking". That is the same shape as the existing\nradio-channel-divergence-undetected entry, and it is arguably the more important\nhalf of this finding.\n\nNOT FIXED — diagnosis needs Peter: it may be physical, and the next step is his\ncall, not a code change.'}
