2026-08-16 18:59:11,014 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'remove-alarm-from-node-dash', 'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'PETER HAS DECIDED. 2026-08-16, on the previous handover\'s line "Peter is\nconsidering moving the alarm out of node-dash entirely": "he has decided".\n\nSo this is no longer a DECIDE. The alarm page and the backend module that manages\nit leave node-dash.\n\nNO SUCH TASK EXISTED. I searched every mcpp task, open and completed, for\nalarm/garage, and every parked one. The nearest were BOUNDARY tasks, not removal:\n  913  browser-plugin-boundary   "Alarm UI must not live in core public/ files"\n  694  custom-app-extension-point\n  630  purge-custom-alarm-code   [completed] - purged alarm NODE MANAGEMENT\n  838  alarm-plugin-boundary-restore [completed]\nPeter believed one existed. It did not, or it is in another project - and\n`active-project-flipped-mid-session` is an open item where nine tasks were\nmis-filed, so that is worth checking before assuming it was never written.\n\nTHE COUPLING, MEASURED 2026-08-16 - AND THE PREVIOUS HANDOVER HAD IT WRONG.\nIt said "core references the alarm in 17 files but 15 are comments". Actual:\nSEVEN core files, and in six of them EVERY reference is a comment:\n\n  src/browser-plugins.js:61   comment\n  src/format.js:106           comment\n  src/node-status.js:36       comment\n  src/observatory.js:202      comment\n  src/observatory-ws.js:3,11  comments\n  src/ws-relay.js:233,250,1242 comments\n\nSo the ONLY real code coupling in core is src/index.js - 12 lines:\n\n  :7        import * as pacHost from \'./alarm-host.js\'\n  :32-34    pacCommandRouter, pacAlignRouter, alarmImageRouter\n  :59-62    side-effect imports of alarm-sections/ws/images/browser\n  :344-346  app.use() x3   (:346 already carries the comment\n                            "delete this line and the plugin is gone")\n  :470      pacHost.start()\n  :240      \'/control\' in the SPA page route list\n\nMODULES TO DELETE (9 files):\n  src/alarm-host.js (49 KB), alarm-sections.js (26 KB), alarm-images.js (18 KB),\n  alarm-image-api.js, alarm-ws.js, alarm-browser.js,\n  src/pac-command-api.js, src/pac-align-api.js\n  and coulomb.js - SEE BELOW, it is the one that is not simple.\n\nTHE BROWSER IS ALREADY CLEAN. Two references in core public/, and BOTH are prose:\n  public/app-ws.js:68            a comment\n  public/partials/tab-cfg.html:600 label text about the rotator hold\nThere is NO tab-control.html partial - the Control page is served by the plugin.\nWhoever did the plugin-boundary work did it properly; this removal is not\nuntangling a browser.\n\nTHE ONE GENUINELY TANGLED THING - src/coulomb.js:\n  coulomb.js:13   imports getObs from \'./alarm-host.js\'\n  coulomb.js:60   uses it\n  BUT it is imported by BOTH sides:\n    src/alarm-sections.js:34  coulombModel   (alarm)\n    src/ws-relay.js:64        buildCoulomb   (CORE)\n  So core depends on a module that depends on the alarm. Deleting alarm-host.js\n  breaks ws-relay.js. coulomb.js must be split, moved, or its core consumer\n  retired - and that decision is step 1, before anything is deleted.\n\nSTORE: obs_observation, obs_fact. Ownership NOT established - find out whether\nthey are the alarm\'s or the observatory\'s before deleting anything. `relay_observation`\nis core (packet provenance) despite the similar name.\n\nDO NOT start deleting from this note. Step 1 exists because coulomb.js and the\nobs_* tables are the two things that will bite.'}
