2026-08-16 23:33:49,700 1418298 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': "One flat file per repo, one script that owns it, closure derived from two runs.\n\nSpec: /root/.claude/docs/specs/idiot-yaml-ssot.md\nProof: python3 /root/.claude/tests/test_idiot_yaml.py\n  before /root/.claude/proofs/idiot-yaml-ssot.before.txt  exit 1, 12 of 12 red\n  after  /root/.claude/proofs/idiot-yaml-ssot.after.txt   exit 0, 12 of 12 green\n\nWhy not specboard, measured rather than assumed: it already has proof/proof_of/proof_needs and\na commit-stamped run table with pass/fail/skip. But 24 of 24 recorded runs are pass — no proof\nthere has ever gone red, so none has been shown able to. That plus the schema being past what\nPeter can follow is the reason for a smaller thing. Both findings belong to specboard's owner\nand go on their channel, not into this file.\n\nScope amended during implementation, stated not done quietly: idiot_gate.py joined the file\nlist, because criterion 1 was declared up front and could not go green while `proof` still\naccepted a typed --before-exit.\n\nFalsification found a hole in the checks themselves: dropping the newer-than-capture rule left\nall 12 green, because check 11 only asserted the closed state. Rewritten to require a closed\nitem to RE-OPEN when the capture is made newer than the source."}
2026-08-16 23:33:51,347 1418298 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_done args={'number': 1}
2026-08-16 23:33:55,017 1418298 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'One file per repo listing every bug and enhancement, with closure derived from a red run and a green run of the same command — not typed by anyone.\n\nIt replaces nothing that works and duplicates nothing that is read: specboard keeps claims, mcpp keeps scheduling, idiot.yaml keeps proof. The constraint that keeps it small is the field set, and adding a field means removing one.'}
