2026-08-16 23:59:02,237 1418298 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'An accusation is tried before it is believed, and the test that convicts is the test that proves the fix.\n\nThe model shipped earlier the same day assumed guilt: idiot.py before threw away a first run that exited 0 as "not a reproduction". A green first run is a verdict, not a bad capture — the claim may be false, or the test may be unable to see the defect, and those are different outcomes that must not be collapsed.\n\nSpec: /root/.claude/docs/specs/idiot-trial-verdict.md\nTrial: /root/.claude/proofs/idiot-trial-verdict.trial.txt  exit 1\nFix:   /root/.claude/proofs/idiot-trial-verdict.fix.txt    exit 0, 21 of 21'}
2026-08-16 23:59:08,989 1418298 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Trial first, then verdict, then the fix — enforced at the hook rather than described in prose.\n\nFalsified five ways. Two did not falsify on the first attempt: the acquittal-reason rule and the files-newer-than-trial rule were both untested, so removing them left every box green. Checks 17 and 18 were written to exercise them. Third time in this work that falsification found a hole in the checks rather than the code.\n\nRetired tests/test_idiot_yaml.py — it tested the before/after contract this replaces. All 12 of its checks map onto the new suite except duplicate-id, carried over as check 19 before deletion.\n\nCheck 0 deleted rather than left green: it asserted that `before` refuses a green run, and once `before` was gone it could only pass vacuously. Its evidence survives in the trial capture.\n\nStill open, recorded as untried accusations in ~/.claude/idiot.yaml:\n  gate-after-exit-can-be-typed    idiot_gate.py after still takes a typed --after-exit\n  run-json-duplicates-idiot-yaml  two files hold one truth'}
