2026-08-17 00:07:34,802 1418298 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'note', 'text': 'Peter, mid-task, verbatim:\n\n"so a tral cannnot be conducted without evidence, and a judgement cannot be made also. so no evidence and no test is not a succes or fail. it is a no trial / retrial with more evidence."\n\nConsequence for the design: a fourth verdict, MISTRIAL. It is not a disposition of the accusation — it says no trial happened. A trial is a mistrial when the test could not be launched, exited 127/126, or produced no evidence at all (an empty capture).\n\nCrucially it grants NOTHING: same permissions as untried. It cannot convict, cannot be acquitted, cannot be waived, and unlocks no file. The only exit is a retrial with a test that actually runs and says something. That is what stops a fourth state becoming the drain every hard case flows into — the earlier objection to a third verdict.\n\nRequiring output, not just an exit code, is the load-bearing half: it is what caught the false conviction in the fair test, where the capture showed a comment AGREEING with the spec.'}
