2026-08-17 07:59:25,948 1496996 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_done args={'number': 1}
2026-08-17 07:59:31,234 1496996 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Eleven proven entries in this repo\'s own register read `guilty`; `idiot list closed` returned 1 of 16. Make closure read the evidence it already records, and make the strength of each closure visible rather than uniform.\n\nNOT the handover\'s diagnosis. It blamed the `cp` that reset every mtime. The real cause is that all eleven name `hooks/idiot.py` — a path that stopped existing when the tree became a repo — and the mtime branch returned a REFUSAL for a path it could not stat, as though the file had said "I did not change". It would fail with mtimes perfectly preserved.\n\nRejected: `close --why`. It records that a human said so, which is strictly less evidence than the trial.at/fix.at pair the tool already wrote down.'}
2026-08-17 07:59:38,437 1496996 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Spec: docs/specs/closure-ignores-recorded-at.md (attached). Register entry: `closure-ignores-recorded-at`, closed on CLOSED/commit.\n\nSeparate "cannot answer" from "no" in every rung, then order them strongest-first; a rung that CAN answer is final.\n  commit  a named file changed between trial.commit and fix.commit\n  mtime   every named file newer than the trial capture — a missing path is NO ANSWER, not a refusal\n  at      fix.at later than trial.at — reached only when the filesystem cannot be asked\n\n`closure_of()` returns which rung answered; `list` prints CLOSED/commit | /at | /mtime | /ruling.\n`now()` moved to millisecond resolution — at second resolution a trial and its fix record the same instant and the pair cannot order itself. An equal pair does not close.\n\nFIRST DRAFT WAS WRONG. Putting `at` above `mtime` made the mtime rung non-binding, and test_idiot_trial.py check 18 went red ("a trial capture newer than the source re-opens a closed item"). The check was not adjusted; the change was corrected to fit it.\n\nFalsified 4 ways against mutated COPIES via IDIOT=, plus an unmutated control: 4 rules falsified, 0 holes. 23/23 trial, 13/13 gate.'}
