2026-08-17 08:18:12,095 1496996 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Peter: "what this repo also lacks is a TERSE functional spec defining what and what not it does, and it\'s purpose, it\'s use of a single idiot.yaml for simplicity. there is simply no point in creating a huge spec file because I will never read it. so we create the terse FUNCTIONAL spec, we then audit what we have against it."\n\nAlso his framing on priority: "cli-styling is not urgent, what is urgent is that what we already have is bug free."\n\nContext that governs the size of this: specboard consumed three days, reached 11,007 lines, and was abandoned for the reason it was created — its bug list became effectively infinite. Peter\'s judgement: there is a very good chance idiot drifts the same way. The spec therefore carries a stopping condition, not just a description.'}
2026-08-17 08:18:15,210 1496996 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_done args={'number': 1}
2026-08-17 08:18:22,040 1496996 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'docs/SPEC.md (attached), one page. Purpose, the loop, verbs, two types, verdicts, closure and its printed strength, the hook, one file, WHAT IT DOES NOT DO, the five properties, stopping condition.\n\nAudit: 18 claims, one command each, run against the real script in throwaway git repos. 15 hold. 3 divergences raised as register entries and deliberately NOT fixed in this pass:\n  hook-prints-an-invocation-that-does-not-work    prints `idiot.py try --id <id>` -> "unrecognized arguments: --id"\n  add-accepts-paths-that-do-not-resolve           --spec and --file pointing at nothing, silently\n  an-entry-with-no-files-can-never-close          empty --file list; closure_of returns None; only surfaces at prove\n\nTrap worth keeping: a bare exit code read through `| head` is head\'s, not the tool\'s. The mistrial-blocks check first read rc=0 that way; run without a pipe it is rc=2.'}
