2026-08-17 09:26:41,276 1496996 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'note', 'text': 'DECIDE — RULED YES, 2026-08-17. Peter, verbatim: "that is a HUGE improvement, it is now readable".\n\nThe gate is passed on the HTML-grid build (c9fd652), NOT on the mermaid one. Mermaid was rejected for the top-level flow because a layout engine decides positions and the requirement is that we decide them.\n\nWhat the build settled that phase DISCUSS was going to argue about:\n  - nodes carry ids; edges reference them by id; position is a declared [col,row] field. The graph-vs-tree objection to yaml nesting never arises because nothing is nested.\n  - the widget set IS the schema. Six types, closed: action, state, decision, gate, terminal, hole.\n  - the type fixes the colour. Red is only `hole`.\n  - the contract is enforced at generation, exit 2, five refusals, all exercised.\n\nWHAT IS STILL UNSOUND, and it is the reason phase TOOL matters: lifecycle.yaml is HAND-WRITTEN. The chart currently asserts "one hole" with nothing checking it. Once red means defect, a hand-drawn chart is a defect count with no test behind it — the exact thing this repo exists to stop. The generator is not a nicety; it is what makes the red count mean anything.'}
