2026-08-17 13:56:51,064 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'remove-alarm-from-node-dash', 'kind': 'note', 'text': 'CORRECTION, 2026-08-16 — I WROTE THIS TASK AS A DELETION AND IT IS NOT ONE.\n\nPeter, on reading it: "remove DOE NOT MEAN DESTROY. the intention is it will run\nas it\'s own pm2 service".\n\nThe goal note above says "MODULES TO DELETE (9 files)" and the old step 4 said\n"delete the modules". BOTH WERE WRONG and both were dangerous — a session acting\non that wording would have destroyed nine working modules including a 49 KB\nalarm-host.js, and the intent was only ever to relocate them.\n\nTHIS IS AN EXTRACTION. The alarm becomes its own pm2 service, alongside node-dash,\nbridge and timelapse-pull. The code MOVES. Nothing is deleted from disk until it\nis running somewhere else and proven.\n\nWHAT THAT CHANGES ABOUT THE WORK:\n\n  - The 8 alarm/pac modules are the new service\'s SOURCE, not scrap. They move\n    largely intact — they already talk to the bridge on :8790 over its own\n    sockets, which is exactly what a standalone service would do.\n  - node-dash\'s job shrinks to: stop hosting it. Unwire the 12 lines in\n    src/index.js and drop \'/control\' from the SPA page list.\n  - THE NEW SERVICE NEEDS ITS OWN EVERYTHING: pm2 entry, port, and a decision\n    about its store. Today the alarm shares node-dash\'s SQLite\n    (data/node-dash.db) — obs_observation and obs_fact live there. A separate\n    service sharing one SQLite file is a design choice, not a default, and\n    `alarm-db-ownership` [completed, PARKED at the time] already asked this\n    question once.\n  - coulomb.js stops being "which side owns it" and becomes an API question:\n    ws-relay.js:64 imports buildCoulomb, so if node-dash still shows a coulomb\n    reading it must ASK the new service for it rather than import a module. That\n    is a smaller and more honest problem than splitting the file.\n\nWHAT DOES NOT CHANGE: step 1 still has to settle coulomb.js and the obs_* tables\nbefore anything moves, and step 2 is still Peter\'s — which repo, which port, and\nwhether node-dash keeps showing anything alarm-shaped at all.\n\nTHE CLASS OF ERROR, because it is the one that matters here: I turned "moving the\nalarm out" into "delete" without checking, and wrote it into a durable task where\nit would have been read as instruction. An extraction and a deletion look similar\nin a summary and are opposites in a repo.'}
2026-08-17 14:01:20,824 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'remove-alarm-from-node-dash', 'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'DESTINATION, given by Peter 2026-08-17: /usr/share/pac/dev/projects/mt-alarm/html\n\nConfirmed to exist. mt-alarm holds: device, device.0, device.1, docs, html,\nplugins, scripts, services.\n\nAND MT-ALARM IS ALREADY THE OTHER HALF OF THIS SYSTEM. The bridge node-dash\nconsumes on :8790 identifies itself as "mt-alarm bridge — The only route to the\nLoRa units. Every frame to and from a device crosses here." So the alarm is not\nbeing moved somewhere new; it is being moved back to where the rest of it already\nlives, and the pieces it talks to are already there.\n\nTHIS MAKES THE EXTRACTION A TWO-REPO JOB, AND ONLY ONE HALF IS NODE-DASH\'S:\n\n  node-dash side (OURS)\n    - unwire src/index.js: the import at :7, three routers at :32-34, four\n      side-effect imports at :59-62, three app.use() at :344-346, pacHost.start()\n      at :470, and \'/control\' from the SPA page list at :240\n    - settle coulomb.js — ws-relay.js:64 imports buildCoulomb. With the alarm on\n      its own service this is an API question (ask it) not a file split\n    - settle obs_observation / obs_fact: they live in data/node-dash.db today\n\n  mt-alarm side (NOT OURS BY DEFAULT)\n    - receive the 8 modules into html/ (or wherever mt-alarm decides)\n    - its own pm2 entry, its own port, its own store decision\n    - serve the Control page it already serves as a plugin\n\nCLAUDE.md, node-dash: "This repo only. Do not read, reference, or modify anything\noutside /usr/share/pac/dev/projects/mt-radar/node-dash/. Cross-repo modification\nis never permitted."\n\nSo the mt-alarm half needs either an mt-alarm session, or Peter\'s explicit\ninstruction to work there. It is NOT something to start unasked. The coordination\npath already exists: the xsession channel `node-dash--plugins` is mt-alarm\'s\nplugin session — the same peer that ships the /plugin/dash/live feeds node-dash\nconsumes.\n\nORDER MATTERS: mt-alarm must be running and serving BEFORE node-dash unwires,\nor the Control page dies in the gap. Nothing is deleted from node-dash until the\nnew service is proven.'}
