2026-08-17 22:15:15,060 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'observatory-decouple-disable', 'title': 'GAP - DISABLE and decouple the Observatory (DISC discovery + Snapshot). DISABLE, NOT DELETE — Peter may reuse parts', 'steps': ['Investigate: the full surface, every core file that imports it, and what stops if the runner stops', 'DISCUSS with Peter: disable at which seam — feature flag, unmount, or unwire — and what happens to the 2.3M stored rows', 'Document', 'Implement: disable at the agreed seam, code left in place', 'Observe: node-dash runs with it off, obs_fact stops growing, every other page unaffected', 'Track']}
2026-08-17 22:15:40,726 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'observatory-decouple-disable', 'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'PETER, 2026-08-17: "there was a whole new module (backend) and frontend created\nfor observatory, aka DISC discover and snapshot. it needs to ve decoupled /\ndisabled NOT deleted. I may re-use parts of it in the future."\n\nDISABLE, NOT DELETE. He has now had to say this twice in one session — the first\ntime about the alarm, where I had written a task up as a deletion. Do not repeat\nit. Nothing is removed from disk. The seam is a switch, not a scalpel.\n\nTHE SURFACE, MEASURED 2026-08-17\n\n  backend                                   bytes\n    inferences.js                          60,591\n    observatory-ws.js                      47,936\n    standing-tasks.js                      47,768\n    mission-runner.js                      41,271\n    snapshot-api.js                        21,937\n    observatory.js                         17,692\n    clusters.js                            16,902\n    doors.js                               13,663\n    hooks.js                                9,277\n    probe-plan.js                           8,773\n    reach.js                                7,702\n    observations.js                         6,982\n    clusters-api.js                         4,190\n    reach-api.js                            2,210\n                                          ~307 KB across 14 modules\n\n  frontend\n    public/partials/tab-observatory.html   71,240\n    public/app-observatory.js              59,103\n    public/partials/tab-snapshot.html      23,921\n    public/app-snapshot.js                  6,305\n                                          ~160 KB across 4 files\n\n  store        obs_observation  549,575 rows\n               obs_fact       1,795,250 rows\n               clusters\n\nTHE DATA IS THE PART THAT SURPRISED PETER, and it is worth its own decision.\nobs_fact is growing ~120,000 rows/day and has been steady all week:\n\n  select date(ts,\'unixepoch\') day, count(*) from obs_fact group by day;\n    08-17 103,302   08-16 130,833   08-15 114,198   08-14 114,619\n    08-13 138,053   08-12 127,319   08-11 110,670\n\n  select key, count(*) from obs_fact group by key order by 2 desc;\n    reach.target    1,055,039\n    link.observed     508,194\n    relay.usage       189,600\n    reach.mission      40,243\n    reach.ladder        1,770\n    reach.heard         1,623\n\nAt ~120k/day that is ~44M rows/year in a store already over 700 MB. Whatever is\ndecided about the code, the WRITE RATE is a separate question and disabling the\nrunner is what actually stops it.\n\nWHAT "DECOUPLED" HAS TO MEAN HERE, and why step 2 is a DISCUSS\n\nThere are at least three different seams and they are not equivalent:\n\n  a) FEATURE FLAG      — the code loads, the runner does not run, the routes 404\n                         or return "disabled". Cheapest to reverse. Leaves the\n                         imports in place, so core still depends on it loading.\n  b) UNMOUNT           — routers not mounted, WS wiring not registered, page\n                         dropped from the SPA list. Code on disk, zero runtime.\n  c) FULL DECOUPLE     — core has no import of it at all; it becomes a plugin or\n                         its own service, like the alarm just did.\n\n(c) is the most work and the most reusable later. (a) is the least and stops the\nrow growth today. Peter\'s words are "decoupled / disabled" — BOTH are named, and\nwhich one he means is exactly what step 2 must ask rather than assume.\n\nDO NOT ASSUME THIS IS THE ALARM AGAIN. The alarm was already decoupled before it\nmoved — 12 wiring lines and comments. The Observatory is NOT: it owns tables that\n`inferences.js` reads, `ws-relay.js` serves its feeds, and DISC is a dash MODE,\nwhich means dash-mode.js and the rotator/mission path are entangled with it.\nStep 1 must measure that entanglement before any seam is chosen.\n\nRELATED, ALREADY OPEN: `dashboard-rethink` (PARKED FOR DISCUSSION — "the\ndashboard needs a re-think"), `board-verdicts`, `board-panel`, `logs-page`,\n`snapshot-board` and about a dozen observatory/board tasks. If the Observatory is\nbeing switched off, several of those become moot or need re-scoping. Check them\nbefore working any of them.'}
2026-08-17 22:49:00,670 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'traceroute-callers-rewrite', 'title': 'DISCUSS - keep traceroute.js, rip out every caller and rebuild the decision layer', 'steps': ["Document: extract traceroute.js's invariants into a spec BEFORE anything is rewritten", 'DISCUSS with Peter: who owns radio and aim — the mode, the caller, or a new dispatcher', 'Document: the new caller contract', 'Implement: one caller at a time, each proven before the next', 'Observe', 'Track']}
2026-08-17 22:49:32,350 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'traceroute-callers-rewrite', 'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'PETER, 2026-08-17: "traceroute.js might be correct in what it does, but the\nimplementation of it is a mess. what I want to do is to leave traceroute.js but\nto rip out all usage of it and start afresh."\n\nSo: src/traceroute.js STAYS. Every CALLER is replaced. The rotten layer is who\ndecides the radio and the aim, not how a traceroute is dispatched and recorded.\n\nWHY THIS BOUNDARY IS THE RIGHT ONE. traceroute.js is mostly scar tissue and each\nscar is a real incident. A blank-page rewrite re-learns them ON AIR:\n  - point() not move() — move() fire-and-forgets; the first version polled status\n    on a timer and could still transmit mid-slew\n  - beam_deg from the TRANSMITTING radio, not the rotator — caught before it\n    stamped 35 deg on rows the OMNI sent\n  - MAC-vs-node_id compare in _recordFailure — a node_id-side compare can never\n    match a MAC device, and it silently skipped the az stamp on every row\n  - send_failed vs timeout as DISTINCT outcomes — otherwise a dead gateway reads\n    as a quiet mesh\n  - startedAt on the pending entry — without it a timeout row cannot say whether\n    it waited 5 s or 90 s\n  - cooldown checked BEFORE the disabled guard, so re-enabling does not skip the\n    next attempt\nKeep all of that. Replace the layer above it.\n\nTHE CALLERS TO REPLACE — measured 2026-08-17, six sites in five files:\n\n  src/passive-tracer.js:252  run(from, {radio: transmitterForMode(\'pasv\',\n                             {rxDevice}), reason:\'passive\'})          PASV\n  src/lifecycle.js:32        run(contact.from, {radio: sender, aim:\'none\',\n                             cooldownMs, cooldownKey, reason:\'scan-contact\'}) SCAN\n  src/lifecycle.js:80        run(num, {radio: sender, aim:\'none\', cooldownMs,\n                             cooldownKey, reason:\'actv-point\'})       ACTV\n  src/mission-runner.js:547  run(to, {... aimCtx ...})                 DISC\n  src/traceroute-api.js:32   run(targetNum, {...})                     manual\n  src/automation.js:200      run(target, {aim:\'endpoint\'})             @route verb\n\n  Importers that do NOT dispatch (leave alone): bridge-events.js (handlePacket),\n  ws-relay.js (feeds).\n\nWHAT IS ACTUALLY BROKEN, and what the new layer must fix\n\n  1. TWO SOURCES OF MODE TRUTH, disagreeing right now:\n       MODE_DEFAULTS (code)        mode_config (DB)\n       pasv.rx  non-rotator        all         <- differ\n       actv.rx  rotator            primary     <- differ\n     Reading the source tells you the wrong thing. Third time this session a\n     stored blob has contradicted correct code.\n\n  2. THE MODE DECLARES `aim` AND NOTHING READS IT. dash-mode owns aim by design\n     and _decideAim exists because "traceroute still points at eps" — but PASV,\n     ACTV and SCAN all pass aim:\'none\' and DISC passes a pre-computed aimCtx.\n     modeAim() has NO production caller. _decideAim — the thinking part, built\n     because endpoint-aiming is wrong 87.1% of the time (n=2,726) — is\n     UNREACHABLE outside the manual API.\n\n  3. THE RADIO IS RESOLVED TWICE. lifecycle.js calls transmitterForMode() and\n     passes the result as opts.radio; run() then skips _resolveRadio because\n     opts.radio is set. Same answer, two entry points, one documented SSOT.\n\n  4. A REAL CONFLICT, not just duplication: _pending is keyed by TARGET ALONE.\n     Two radios tracing the same node share one entry — the second JOINS the\n     first and both resolve on the first radio\'s result with the first radio\'s\n     device. Two radios cannot independently measure the same target.\n\n  5. pasv.rx=\'all\' means the passive tracer transmits on the DIRECTIONAL YAGI at\n     whatever azimuth it is sitting at. Confirmed live: both radios pass the pasv\n     listener gate, and transmitterForMode(\'pasv\', {rxDevice: YAGI}) returns the\n     YAGI. 114 YAGI dispatches in 24 h, every one aim_mode=\'none\'.\n\nSTEP 1 IS A SPEC, NOT CODE, and that is deliberate. The invariants above exist\nONLY as comments inside the file whose callers are being deleted. Extract them —\nincident, rule, and the check that proves it — so the rewrite has something to be\ncorrect AGAINST. "Start afresh" without that means starting without the six\nguards listed at the top.\n\nSTEP 2 IS THE DESIGN CALL AND IT IS PETER\'S: does the MODE own radio+aim (fix\ndash-mode and make callers stop overriding), does the CALLER own it (delete the\nmode\'s aim/radio declarations as dead), or does a new dispatcher sit between?\nDo not choose this alone — the current mess is precisely what happens when the\nanswer is "both".\n\nNOTE: DISC is currently INERT. missionRunner.setQueue() is called from inside the\nobservatory block disabled in 3b39449, so mission-runner dispatches nothing.\nWhoever works this must not read "DISC does nothing" as evidence about DISC.'}
