2026-08-17 22:51:43,969 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'traceroute-callers-rewrite', 'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'SEQUENCING — PETER, 2026-08-17, and it is a rule not a preference:\n\n  "no re-implementation logic will be decided until all existing calls to it are\n   completely removed from code. then we will decide how it will work"\n\nSo this task is REMOVAL ONLY. It does not design the replacement, does not\npropose one, and does not leave a stub that hints at one. The design conversation\nhappens AFTER the tree is clean, as its own task, on a blank field.\n\nThe earlier version of this plan had "DISCUSS who owns radio and aim" as step 2.\nThat is now WRONG and has been removed: deciding while the old callers are still\nin front of us is exactly how the current design got argued into existence.\n\nWHAT GOES — six sites, five files:\n  passive-tracer.js:252   PASV\n  lifecycle.js:32         SCAN contact\n  lifecycle.js:80         ACTV point_target\n  mission-runner.js:547   DISC (already inert — see below)\n  traceroute-api.js:32    manual REST\n  automation.js:200       the @route verb\n\nWHAT STAYS, UNTOUCHED:\n  src/traceroute.js       every line. Peter: "traceroute.js might be correct in\n                          what it does, but the implementation of it is a mess."\n                          The mess is the callers.\n  bridge-events.js        handlePacket — decodes REPLIES. It imports traceroute\n                          but does not dispatch. With nothing dispatching it will\n                          simply never match a pending entry.\n  ws-relay.js             traceroute_history feeds. Reading, not dispatching.\n\nTHE OPERATIONAL CONSEQUENCE, stated plainly because it is large:\n\n  NODE-DASH WILL DISPATCH NO TRACEROUTES AT ALL. No route discovery, no verified\n  hop counts, no new traceroute_history rows. Existing rows stay; they simply\n  stop being added to. Passive tracing stops. The @route verb stops answering.\n  Anything downstream that reads "verified hops" gets progressively staler with\n  no signal that it is doing so.\n\n  That is the intended state, not a regression — but it is a state the dashboard\n  does not currently announce anywhere, and nobody should discover it by noticing\n  a number has not moved.\n\nALREADY INERT, so do not read its silence as evidence: DISC. missionRunner is fed\nfrom inside the observatory block disabled in 3b39449.\n\nWHAT THE REMOVAL MUST NOT DO:\n  - leave a commented-out call as a "reminder". Git has it.\n  - leave a no-op wrapper or a feature flag that could be flipped back on. Peter\n    asked for the calls REMOVED, and a dormant path is not removed.\n  - silently change what the surrounding function does. lifecycle.js:32 and :80\n    still have their scan-contact and point_target handlers — those keep their\n    other work (confirmScanContact, the tracker\'s own bookkeeping); only the\n    dispatch leaves.\n\nSTEP 1 EXISTS BECAUSE THE LIST MAY BE INCOMPLETE. The six above are static\n`traceroute.run(` matches. Confirm there is no dynamic dispatch, no\n`bridge.post(\'/…/traceroute\')` bypassing the module (lifecycle.js:74 has one\nbehind the FF.SSOT_TRACEROUTE legacy branch), and nothing in public/ POSTing to\nthe manual route.'}
