2026-08-17 22:58:16,855 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'note', 'text': 'SWEEP RESULT — the list was SIX, it is SEVEN. 2026-08-17, after removing the six.\n\nThe seventh was invisible to every `traceroute.run(` grep because it is not a\ncall to traceroute.js at all:\n\n  src/op-manager.js:286  op \'send_traceroute\'\n                         method POST, endpoint p => `/${p.target}/traceroute`\n\nop-manager\'s catalogue is driven GENERICALLY — nothing in src/ names the op — so\nit survived three sweeps. Its endpoint is node-dash\'s own manual route, which\nstep 3 deleted, so from that moment it could only 404 while reporting a failed\n`http_200` confirmation: an op-manager fault indistinguishable from a dead radio.\n\nRemoved, with its two dependents:\n  tests/test_ops.py           it was in SKIP_OPS; you cannot skip an op that is gone\n  docs/modules/op-manager.md  the ops table row\n\nTHE LESSON, for the rewrite: a dispatch path can exist as DATA. Grepping for the\nfunction name finds code, not catalogue entries, config blobs or stored rows. The\nnext sweep of anything must also grep for the ROUTE STRING, which is what caught\nthis one.\n\nWHAT NOW IMPORTS traceroute.js — two files, both verified non-dispatching:\n  bridge-events.js:5   handlePacket() — DECODES replies we overhear. Must stay,\n                       or passive route data is lost as well as active.\n  ws-relay.js:62       .on(\'result\'/\'aiming\'/\'aimed\'/\'start\'/\'cancel\') — listeners\n                       only. Inert now that nothing dispatches. Left in place\n                       deliberately: they are the browser\'s feed contract, and\n                       cutting them is Domain 2 work, not this task\'s.\n\nSTILL LIVE, AND NOT THIS TASK\'S DOMAIN — two browser callers POST to the route\nthat no longer exists, so both now 404:\n  public/app-perf.js:80     auto-traceroute scheduler\n  public/app-radar.js:1233  the radar TRACE button\nCLAUDE.md: "No fix may span domains in a single task." Raised as its own Domain 2\ntask rather than being fixed here.'}
