2026-08-17 23:38:15,707 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'note', 'name': 'bugs', 'text': 'B-REACH-STALE — CONFIRMED — the reach model now runs on frozen evidence\n\nsrc/reach.js:81,86 read `traceroute_history` for two of the reach model\'s\nevidence classes:\n  first-hop   `json_extract(route,\'$[0]\')` — our transmission reached that relay\n  0-relay     a completed traceroute with an EMPTY route — we reached the endpoint\n\nNothing writes new rows as of 2026-08-17 (commits 2ef5611, 86400ab, c297b9d,\neec402d removed every dispatcher and both decoders). The reach model keeps\nworking and keeps serving `reach_model` on the WS, but its traceroute-derived\nevidence is now fixed at whatever the table held on 2026-08-17 — 37,424 rows,\nnewest 22:57:06 — and will never grow again.\n\nNOT FIXED, DELIBERATELY. It is not traceroute machinery; it is an analytic\nconsumer of the rows Peter chose to keep ("keep the data, drop the reads" — the\nreads he named were the REST GET, the WS history feed and the browser history\npanel). Removing these two would take the reach model with it, which nobody\nasked for.\n\nWHAT IS NOT KNOWN: whether the reach page shows any freshness signal for this.\nIf it does not, the model will look current while its traceroute half silently\nages — the same failure class as the "traceroute-verified" hop badge that was\nremoved for exactly this reason. Not checked.\n\nNaturally resolved by whatever replaces the dispatcher; until then it is a\nstale-data risk, not a broken one.'}
