2026-08-17 23:59:13,018 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': "Executed under /afk, all five /idiot phases without pausing. Spec:\ndocs/modules/radio-resolve-and-aim.md (attached). Commit 4971d77.\n\nWHAT WAS DONE\n\n  NEW src/resolve.js   resolveRadio(spec, ctx) -> { mac, node_id, label,\n                       beam_deg, directional, steerable, rotatorId, channels }.\n                       Specs: MAC | !hex | 'rotator' | 'non-rotator' | 'primary'\n                       | 'auto'. Delegates channels to channels.js.\n  NEW src/aim.js       decideAim() (pure policy, four rules + evidence intact),\n                       aimAt() (the ONLY rotator.point() caller in this path),\n                       resolveAim() (decide + act -> row provenance),\n                       bearingToNode() moved verbatim.\n  rotator.js           owns HOLD_CEILING_MS (120 s) and clamps `hold` in point().\n  config-api.js        DISCOVERY_LIMITS.hold_sec[1] imported from rotator.js.\n  traceroute.js        _resolveRadio, _decideAim, _resolveAim, _txIsRotator,\n                       toMac, beamwidthFor, bearingToNode all deleted. run()\n                       calls resolveRadio() then resolveAim().\n  tests                test_resolve.mjs (31), test_aim.mjs (28), both in\n                       scripts/check_all.mjs.\n\nTHE THREE FALSIFICATIONS, each shown failing and then restored:\n  non-rotator returning the rotator   -> test_resolve FAILS\n  hold clamp removed from point()     -> test_aim FAILS (999999999 vs 120000)\n  aimAt steerable gate removed        -> test_aim FAILS (it pointed)\n\nWHAT IS STILL OPEN, for a waking session:\n\n  1. NOTHING CALLS traceroute.run() — still deliberately unwired. This task\n     restructured it; it did not re-wire it. Peter's sequencing rule stands: the\n     replacement's dispatch policy is decided on a clean tree.\n\n  2. NO RF AND NO ROTATOR MOVEMENT WAS EXERCISED. The two tests that reach\n     point() stub the rotator's transport. A traceroute cannot be dispatched\n     without putting a frame on air on a channel we do not choose, and pointing\n     moves an antenna shared with the garage alarm.\n\n  3. THE CHANNEL QUESTION IS UNANSWERED AND BELONGS TO ANOTHER REPO. mesh-gw's\n     send_traceroute(to) takes no channel (docs/gw/modules/ble_device.md:66), so\n     the firmware picks. If it picks PRIMARY, every traceroute node-dash ever\n     sent went out on the public mesh. Ask the DEVICE, not the docs, via\n     xsession — mt-transport/mesh-gw's call, not ours.\n\n  4. traceroute still READS rotator.status.az when stamping rotator_az on a row\n     (two sites). That is a read, not a command, but it is arguably provenance\n     aim already returns as az_actual. Left alone to keep this task's scope\n     honest; recorded in the bugs ledger rather than fixed in flight."}
