2026-08-18 00:00:07,010 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'note', 'name': 'bugs', 'text': 'RULINGS on four entries filed earlier today, 2026-08-17. Commit 4971d77.\n\n── traceroute-omni-branch-can-return-the-rotator ── FIXED\n\n_resolveRadio() is deleted; src/resolve.js is the SSOT and its \'non-rotator\'\nspec is the lookup the old branch claimed it could not do.\n\nFALSIFICATION RUN, not just asserted: reinstated the defect (made\n`nonRotatorMac()` return `getRotatorAddress()`), ran tests/test_resolve.mjs and\nsaw it FAIL —\n\n    AssertionError: non-rotator must NOT return the rotator — the 2026-08-17 defect\n      actual: \'F4:12:FA:39:F7:B6\'   expected: \'E9:B0:3F:17:27:91\'\n\nthen restored and saw 31 checks pass. The test is reached.\n\n── shared-rotator-hold-ceiling-lives-in-the-caller ── FIXED\n\nHOLD_CEILING_MS now lives in src/rotator.js and point() clamps every caller;\nconfig-api imports it for DISCOVERY_LIMITS.hold_sec so the form cannot drift.\n\nFALSIFICATION: removed the clamp, ran tests/test_aim.mjs, saw it FAIL —\n\n    AssertionError: an absurd hold is clamped to the ceiling\n      actual: 999999999   expected: 120000\n\ni.e. without it an 11.5-day hold reaches a rotator shared with the garage alarm.\nRestored; 28 checks pass.\n\nSTILL NOT KNOWN, and I did not check: whether any OTHER caller currently passes a\nhold at all. The fix makes the question harmless, not answered.\n\n── directionality-is-two-fields-that-can-disagree ── PARTIALLY FIXED\n\nresolve.js now reports them as the two DIFFERENT questions they are —\n`directional` from beam_deg (Peter\'s "360 = omni" test) and `steerable` from\nis_rotator — so a fixed directional antenna is expressible for the first time,\nand test_resolve asserts that case.\n\nNOT fixed: device-config still stores two independent fields with nothing keeping\nthem consistent. Nothing warns if a radio is configured beam_deg 35 with\nis_rotator false by mistake. Left open deliberately — a validation rule on the\ndevice-config form is its own change, and inventing one at 3am while Peter is\nasleep is the kind of decision that should wait.\n\n── three-vocabularies-for-which-radio ── PARTIALLY FIXED\n\ntraceroute\'s private auto|yagi|omni set is gone. resolve.js deliberately reuses\ndash-mode\'s existing words (\'rotator\', \'non-rotator\', \'primary\') rather than\nadding a fourth, and test_resolve fails if \'omni\'/\'yagi\' reappear in RADIO_SPECS.\n\nNOT fixed: dash-mode\'s TX_ROLES/RX_ROLES and resolve.js\'s RADIO_SPECS are still\ntwo lists that happen to agree. Making one derive from the other is a small\nchange but touches the mode config form\'s vocabulary, so it is a waking-hours\ndecision.\n\n── NEW, filed now ──\n\n── traceroute-reads-rotator-status-for-row-provenance ── CONFIRMED, low severity\n\nsrc/traceroute.js still reads `rotator.status.az` at two sites when stamping\n`rotator_az` onto a stored row. It is a READ, not a command, so it does not\nviolate the "aim owns the pointer" boundary in the way _resolveAim did — but it\nis provenance that src/aim.js already returns as `az_actual`, so the row can be\nstamped from two different sources depending on the path taken.\n\nNot fixed in flight: it was outside the attached spec\'s file list for that task,\nand expanding scope mid-implementation is the rule CLAUDE.md exists to stop.'}
