2026-08-18 00:03:20,365 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Opening the Range tab threw `TypeError: this._startRangeAutoSync is not a\nfunction`. app-nav.js:77 called it; it is defined nowhere in public/ and never\nhas been.\n\nPRE-EXISTING, established before fixing: present at 3b39449, and\n`grep -c _startRangeAutoSync public/app-range.js` = 0 there too. Not caused by\nthe traceroute work done the same night.\n\nCOST: setNav() runs the plugin onTab loop AFTER the per-tab chain, so the throw\naborted setNav before any plugin range hook ran. `this.tab = t` and both range\nloaders had already executed, so the page looked correct — which is how a hard\nthrow survived unnoticed. The console-error count read 0 throughout, because the\nthrow happens inside an Alpine handler that swallows it; it only surfaced when\nevery tab was walked with a try/catch per tab.\n\nFIX: delete the call. Not replaced with an implementation — "auto sync" means a\npoll, range state already arrives on the WS (range_test_log, range_test_timer,\nreplayed on connect), and writing the function would introduce the timer the\nstanding "NO TIMERS, NO POLLING FULL STOP" rule forbids.'}
