2026-08-18 06:49:14,727 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'note', 'name': 'bugs', 'text': "pasv-config-has-no-consumer — CONFIRMED, tidy not defect\n\n`pasvConfig()` and `PASV_DEFAULTS` (src/config-api.js:201, :218) lost their last\nconsumer on 2026-08-18, commit 304482a. Their only reader was\nsrc/traceroute.js:271, which now reads the correctly-named\n`traceroute.timeout_sec` instead.\n\nThey are named for PASV — the passive tracer — which was DELETED on 2026-08-17\n(commit c297b9d). So the object is now a defaults table for a mode that does\nnothing, holding a timeout that something else owns.\n\nNOT REMOVED IN FLIGHT, deliberately: `pasv_config` may still be written by the\nconfig form and rendered somewhere, so deleting it is a surface change rather\nthan a dead-code sweep, and expanding scope mid-task is the rule CLAUDE.md exists\nto enforce.\n\nWHAT IS NOT KNOWN: whether anything in public/ still reads or writes pasv_config.\nNot checked — the Config page's PASV card was replaced on 2026-08-17 but the key\nitself was not traced.\n\nCheap when someone picks it up: grep pasv_config across public/ and the config\nform, then delete PASV_DEFAULTS, pasvConfig() and the stored key together."}
