2026-08-18 09:05:53,987 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Peter, 2026-08-18: "that finding is not something to be glossed over. a Prominant comment needs adding to docs and to the resolver so that mistake is never made again."\n\nTHE FINDING. On 2026-08-16 the YAGI was found with its PRIMARY channel misnamed `Public`. docs/modules/channels.md correctly recorded that "a primary renamed `Public` is a channel nothing else on the mesh is listening to" — and then the fix was applied BACKWARDS: `channels.pub_key` was set to b7ecd210 = channelKey(\'Public\',\'AQ==\'), the BROKEN channel, and OMNI (recorded in that same table as *(unnamed)*, key 865e781a) was renamed onto it.\n\nBoth radios then transmitted and listened on a channel no one else uses. Cost: all public traffic dead from 16 Aug ~18:15 (text messages 85/day -> 0, nodeinfo refreshes 185 -> 0, every remote traceroute timing out, and Peter\'s own public messages getting no replies for two days). It was invisible because the radios and the config agreed with each other -- divergences() compares radios to OUR designation, never to the mesh.\n\nFirmware fact that makes the name load-bearing, read from Channels.cpp not from docs:\n  generateHash() = xorHash(getName(ch)) ^ xorHash(key)\n  getName() substitutes the modem preset name ("LongFast") when the stored name is EMPTY and use_preset is set.\nSo empty == "LongFast" == the default channel; ANY other string is a private channel of one. The name is hashed verbatim -- a typo is a different mesh.\n\nSCOPE: comment + doc only. The config value and the radio rename are Peter\'s, in flight now. The channelKey empty->preset substitution defect and the "no public payload decoded in N hours" alarm are SEPARATE tasks, not this one.'}
