2026-08-18 09:08:07,051 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Comment + doc only. No behaviour change. Two files:\n\n1. src/channels.js — a banner block after the existing name+key identity block and\n   before the imports, headed "A MISNAMED PRIMARY IS FIXED BY RENAMING THE RADIO.\n   NEVER BY DESIGNATING IT." Carries: what was done backwards (pub_key set to\n   b7ecd210, OMNI renamed onto it), the measured cost, why divergences() stayed\n   silent (it compares radios to OUR designation, never to the mesh), the\n   recognition signature (you hear everyone, you decrypt no stranger), the rule\n   (the designation names the channel THE MESH is on), and the firmware quote\n   showing getName() substitutes the preset name for an empty name.\n\n2. docs/modules/channels.md — the same content as a marked section between\n   "A channel\'s identity" and "Roles", with the cost as a table.\n\nThen bump source_hash for channels (0ac605be) and run check_specs.\n\nNOT IN SCOPE, deliberately, each its own task:\n - changing channels.pub_key to 865e781a (must follow Peter\'s radio rename)\n - the channelKey() empty->preset substitution defect: node-dash hashes the RAW\n   stored name, so it would call "" and "LongFast" different channels when the\n   firmware treats them as one\n - an alarm for "no public payload decoded in N hours", which is the check that\n   would actually have caught this\n - putting real name+key pairs in config instead of opaque fingerprints (Peter\'s\n   instruction, 2026-08-18)'}
