2026-08-18 09:16:24,396 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'BUG - traceroute.handlePacket() was called by nothing, so every traceroute ran to its full timeout regardless of radio, target or mesh.\n\nFound by testing Peter\'s instinct, 2026-08-18: "my gut feeling tells me there is nothing wrong with either RADIO, this is a node-dash issue." He was right, and it broke a tie the evidence could not: a broken decoder and a silent mesh produce identical evidence.\n\nBoth call sites were removed in c297b9d (2026-08-17) — correct at the time, because every dispatcher had gone and a decoder had nothing to match. Dispatch returned the next day as POST /traceroute and the decode did not return with it.\n\nFIXED and FALSIFIED, committed aba1ee3.\n\nIMPORTANT — this was not the only fault and did not cause the collapse. Underneath it, both radios had been sitting on a misnamed primary channel since 2026-08-16 (fix + warning in 4a9b90b; Peter unset both radio names 2026-08-18). Two independent faults, one symptom. With both fixed, T4 answered at 7469ms after 17 consecutive failures since 15 Aug, and we decode third-party public payloads again (6 strangers, 15 payloads, zero undecodable, vs 1 stranger and zero payloads before).'}
