2026-08-18 09:17:24,707 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Peter, 2026-08-18: "AQ== (or whatever is the PKC for public) and our PRIVATE key should be in our config file. resolver MUST use these to determine the PUBLIC and PRIVATE channel for each radio."\n\nTHE GAP. `channels.pub_key` and `channels.pri_key` are the resolver\'s SSOT and are NOT declared in config-api.js DEFAULTS. Measured 2026-08-18: GET and PUT /config/channels.pub_key both return 404 "Unknown config key". They exist only as rows in the config table, holding a bare sha256 — `b7ecd210d6cd…` — which nobody can read, check, or correct through any interface.\n\nThat opacity is what let the 16 Aug fault survive: a human looking at `b7ecd210…` cannot see it is wrong, whereas `name: "Public"` is wrong at a glance. The value was the MISNAMED channel and stayed there for two days, killing all public traffic. See task channels-misnamed-primary-warning and commit 4a9b90b.\n\nWHAT CHANGES. Config carries the readable pair per role — name AND psk — and `designatedKey(role)` derives channelKey(name, psk) from them instead of reading a stored fingerprint.\n\nSECRECY, decided under /afk and reversible. GET /config returns every DEFAULTS key raw to the browser (config-api.js:204), and the browser makes zero channel decisions (BROWSER_CONTRACT), so it needs neither key:\n - pub_name \'\' / pub_psk \'AQ==\' are the well-known Meshtastic default, not secret, safe as source defaults.\n - pri_name / pri_psk default to NULL. The private PSK is never committed to git and must be configured at runtime.\n - all four are withheld from the GET /config response.\n\nNOT IN SCOPE, its own task: the channelKey() empty->preset substitution. The firmware\'s getName() replaces an empty stored name with the modem preset name ("LongFast") before hashing, so "" and "LongFast" are ONE channel on air and TWO to this resolver.'}
