2026-08-18 09:23:21,235 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': '`node scripts/check_all.mjs` reports RESULT: FAIL with 2 failures, and neither is a defect in the code.\n\n1. tests/test_node.py:125 — "traceroute.js: typed traceroute event not handled in index.js". It greps index.js for the handler. The handler is in src/bridge-events.js, which index.js registers via registerBridgeEvents(bridge); it has never lived in index.js. Restored and PROVEN working 2026-08-18 (commit aba1ee3, falsified: present 3428ms / removed timeout / restored 2375ms). The check asserts the wrong FILE.\n\n2. tests/test_node.py:238,254 — WS:traceroute_history "required on connect but never received". That replay was DELIBERATELY REMOVED on 2026-08-17, task traceroute-remove-backend-remainder; src/ws-relay.js:1279 carries the removal comment. The check still demands it.\n\nWHY THIS MATTERS RATHER THAN BEING COSMETIC: a suite that is permanently red trains everyone to ignore it, and the next real regression lands in a sea of expected failures. This project has already been bitten by a check that ran and proved nothing (check_v2_v3_sync.py, invoked by nothing while v2 and v3 drifted).\n\nREQUIREMENT ON THE FIX: each corrected check must still FAIL if the real behaviour regresses. Deleting the assertions is not acceptable — check 1 must fail if the decode wiring is removed again (which is the exact fault that cost 2026-08-18), and check 2 must fail if a required WS replay genuinely stops arriving.'}
