2026-08-18 09:46:44,751 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'note', 'text': 'CORRECTION — the central claim in this task\'s goal note is WRONG, and it was mine.\n\nThe goal note says the dashboard "paints it 41 hours stale and filters it out of a \'heard\nrecently\' view ONE MINUTE after we received a packet from it", citing filters.js:84,\nfilters.js:91 and ws-relay.js:481.\n\nMEASURED ON THE LIVE WS FEED, 2026-08-18 ~09:20 — it does not:\n\n  T4    last_heard = 33 min ago    tone=warning\n  trac  last_heard = 14 min ago    tone=muted\n  G1    last_heard = 11 min ago    tone=muted\n\nThose are the FIRST-HAND values. The live node list never showed 42.8 h / 558 h / 274.9 h.\nnode-list.js\'s in-memory cache is updated by touchLastHeard() on every received packet\n(bridge-events.js:63), and hydrateFromStore seeds it with `rf_last_heard ?? last_heard`\n(node-list.js:411). The stale figures are in the `nodes` TABLE columns, which the live\npayload does not read for this.\n\nHOW I GOT IT WRONG: I reasoned from the DB columns and from filters.js, and never opened the\npayload the browser actually receives. Same class of error as the traceroute diagnosis\nearlier today — a plausible chain from the wrong layer. "Verification must match the claim."\n\nWHAT IS ACTUALLY TRUE, all verified this turn:\n\n1. queryNodes() in src/filters.js has ZERO CALLERS. Dead code. My whole first implementation\n   attempt edited a function nothing runs; reverted (git checkout, tree clean).\n\n2. queryNodes() would THROW if anything called it. It references `mqtt_nodeinfo`, a table\n   that DOES NOT EXIST in data/node-dash.db, and `node_filters.hide_mqtt` is set TRUE in\n   config — so the branch is live-but-unreachable. SQLITE_ERROR: no such table.\n\n3. queryMessages() in the SAME file has the same reference (filters.js:17) and IS live\n   (index.js:266, ws-relay.js:636). It works today only because `message_filter.hide_mqtt`\n   is unset and defaults false. Turning that toggle on in the UI would 500 the Messages\n   page. A landmine, not a current outage.\n\n4. last_trace_attempt / last_trace_hit ARE genuinely unexposed — confirmed on the live\n   payload, zero keys matching /trace/i on a node. Peter\'s original point stands, and this\n   is the part of the task that is real.\n\n5. The naming complaint stands but is LATENT, not live: nodes.last_heard is the radio\'s\n   second-hand nodedb claim wearing a first-hand name. Nothing user-facing reads it for\n   freshness today, so renaming it is tidiness plus future-proofing, not a bug fix.\n\nRE-SCOPED. This task should do (4) and nothing else. (1)(2)(3) are a separate defect about\ndead code and a missing table, and go to the ledger. The five-timestamps observation remains\ncorrect and worth documenting; the "decisions are bound to the weakest one" conclusion drawn\nfrom it does not.\n\ndocs/modules/node-recency-ssot.md as written also asserts the wrong claim and must be\nrewritten before it is used — it is currently untracked and uncommitted.'}
2026-08-18 09:47:09,350 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'bugs', 'kind': 'note', 'text': '[filters-mqtt-nodeinfo-table-never-existed] CONFIRMED — src/filters.js:17 and :100\n\nBoth filter builders in src/filters.js reference a table `mqtt_nodeinfo` that DOES NOT EXIST\nin data/node-dash.db (verified 2026-08-18 via .tables — zero matches).\n\n  filters.js:17   queryMessages()  `from_num NOT IN (SELECT num FROM mqtt_nodeinfo)`\n                  fires when message_filter.hide_mqtt is true\n  filters.js:100  queryNodes()     `num NOT IN (SELECT num FROM mqtt_nodeinfo WHERE num IS NOT NULL)`\n                  fires when node_filters.hide_mqtt is true\n\nEVIDENCE: calling queryNodes() with the current config throws\n  SqliteError: no such table: mqtt_nodeinfo\nbecause `node_filters.hide_mqtt` is set TRUE in the config table.\n\nSEVERITY IS SPLIT, and the split is the point:\n\n - queryNodes() is DEAD — zero callers anywhere in src/ or public/ (grep, 2026-08-18). So\n   its broken branch harms nothing today. It is also why nobody has noticed.\n - queryMessages() IS LIVE (index.js:266, ws-relay.js:636) and works ONLY because\n   `message_filter.hide_mqtt` is unset and defaults to false. Turning that toggle on in the\n   UI would 500 the Messages page and the message_history WS replay. A LANDMINE, not a\n   current outage.\n\nRELATED, ALREADY KNOWN: config-api.js\'s own comment on node_filters.hide_mqtt says "hide_mqtt\nabove tests a via_mqtt column that does not exist and has always been dead" — so the deadness\nwas known for the NODE filter and the same defect in the MESSAGE filter was not spotted, nor\nwas the fact that the table (not just a column) is absent.\n\nNOT YET DECIDED, needs a call: whether MQTT provenance should be reinstated (there IS a\nrelay_observation table and an ev.via_mqtt flag that persist.js already reads) or whether\nboth toggles and queryNodes() should be deleted. Do not "fix" by creating an empty\nmqtt_nodeinfo table — that would make both filters silently no-ops, which is worse than\nthrowing.\n\nFound while investigating park-node-recency-no-ssot; out of that task\'s scope.'}
