js:11,\n  app-nodes.js:170, app-ws.js:105) and is currently ON. In node-filter.js:82 it tests\n  `node.via_mqtt`, which is never populated — a permanent NO-OP, but plain JS, so it\n  cannot throw. Removing the toggle is a Domain 2 change and cannot share a task with\n  this one (CLAUDE.md). It IS misleading — Peter believes MQTT nodes are being hidden by\n  it when hide_mqtt_only is doing that work — so it needs its own task and his call on\n  whether MQTT provenance gets reinstated properly (relay_observation and ev.via_mqtt\n  exist) or the control is removed.\n\nDO NOT "FIX" BY CREATING AN EMPTY mqtt_nodeinfo TABLE. That would turn both filters into\nsilent no-ops, which is strictly worse than throwing: a filter that quietly matches nothing\nis how you get a page that looks filtered and is not.'}
