2026-08-18 11:52:24,760 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'bugs', 'kind': 'note', 'text': '[owner-form-shows-CLIENT-radio-holds-CLIENT_BASE] CONFIRMED — Devices > radio > Owner\n\nThe Owner form renders ROLE = "CLIENT" for the OMNI. The radio actually holds\nrole = CLIENT_BASE. Measured 2026-08-18, both from the live system:\n\n  GET /!2687afb1/owner  (mesh-gw\'s cooked endpoint, what the form loads)\n      {"short_name":"TA2o","long_name":"TA26 OMNI","__reboot":true,"__notes":[...]}\n      -> NO role field at all\n\n  admin get_owner_request, want_response=true (the radio\'s own answer)\n      {"id":"!2687afb1","long_name":"TA26 OMNI","short_name":"TA2o",\n       "hw_model":"RAK4631","role":"CLIENT_BASE", ...}\n      -> role IS present, and it is CLIENT_BASE\n\nSo the cooked GET drops `role`, the form falls back to its default of \'CLIENT\',\nand the operator is shown a role the radio does not have.\n\nWHY IT HAS NOT CAUSED DAMAGE — by luck, not design. public/app-config.js saveOwner\ndoes:\n\n    const currentRole = this.ownerData?.role ?? \'CLIENT\';\n    if (payload.role === currentRole) delete payload.role;\n\nownerData.role is undefined (dropped by the GET), so currentRole computes to\n\'CLIENT\', the form\'s displayed value is also \'CLIENT\', they compare equal, and\nrole is stripped from the payload. The write therefore does not touch role. Change\neither half of that coincidence — a different default, a form that sends role\nunconditionally — and saving the Owner tab DEMOTES the radio from CLIENT_BASE to\nCLIENT.\n\nThat is the same shape as the 2026-08-04 failure (a role write that reported\nsuccess and did not stick) and the 2026-08-16 channel rename: an operator acting\non a screen that does not show what the radio holds.\n\nNOT FIXED HERE. Found while verifying the radio-config rewrite (commit 8363e62)\nand outside its scope — the rewrite replaced the WRITE path; this is the READ that\npopulates the form. Two possible fixes and they are not equivalent:\n  (a) node-dash loads the Owner form from a genuine admin get_owner_request rather\n      than the cooked GET. Correct, ~471 ms, and no dependency on mesh-gw.\n  (b) mesh-gw stops dropping role from GET /owner. Also correct, and consistent\n      with their current direction of removing cooked surfaces that lose\n      information — worth telling them either way.\n\nPrefer (a): it does not wait on another repo, and the form showing what the RADIO\nholds is the property we actually want.'}
