2026-08-18 12:16:19,274 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'PETER, 2026-08-18, VERBATIM:\n\n"my guess is you did a 1 time export of the schema. this should be a script"\n\nCORRECT, and worse than he guessed.\n\nWHAT I ACTUALLY DID. I read Meshtastic-Android\'s FixedUpdateIntervals.kt once and\ntyped the tables into src/interval-options.js by hand. Nothing re-derives them and\nnothing checks them.\n\nAND THE INPUT IS ABOUT TO VANISH. The only copy of the Kotlin on this machine is\n  /tmp/claude-0/.../<session-id>/scratchpad/FixedUpdateIntervals.kt\na session-scoped temp directory. `find / -name FixedUpdateIntervals.kt` returns\nthat one path and nothing else. So the file is not merely unverified — once this\nsession ends it becomes UNVERIFIABLE, and the numbers in src/ turn into folklore\nwith a citation.\n\nWHAT THE TRANSCRIPTION GOT WRONG, found by checking all 16 lists by hand against\nthe source:\n\n  15 of 16 configurations are byte-for-byte correct.\n\n  ALL is WRONG. The app defines it as `FixedUpdateIntervals.entries` — enum\n  DECLARATION order — and the enum ends:\n\n      ...\n      SEVENTY_TWO_HOURS(72.hours...),\n      ALWAYS_ON(Int.MAX_VALUE.toLong(), ...),\n      EIGHTY_SECONDS(80.seconds...),\n      NINETY_SECONDS(90.seconds...),\n      EIGHT_SECONDS(8.seconds...),\n      FORTY_SECONDS(40.seconds...),\n\n  Four members were appended after ALWAYS_ON, so the app\'s real order ends\n  ... 259200, 2147483647, 80, 90, 8, 40.\n\n  I wrote it ASCENDING. Same 34 values, different order. I tidied.\n\nTHAT IS THE SIGNATURE FAILURE OF A HAND-TRANSCRIPTION, and it is the argument for\nthe script better than any principle: the error is not a typo, which review would\ncatch. It is an improvement. I made the data more sensible than the source, which\nis precisely what a port must never do, and no test could have caught it because\nevery test I wrote asserts the values I typed.\n\nHarmless TODAY only by luck: ALL is mapped to no field in FIELD_CONFIGURATION, so\nnothing renders from it. Luck is not a property worth relying on.\n\nDECISION: the tables become GENERATED OUTPUT from a source vendored INTO the repo,\nwith a check that fails when the two disagree. Not a doc rule, not a review habit —\na check that goes red.'}
