2026-08-18 12:27:37,079 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'bugs', 'kind': 'note', 'text': 'select-controls-have-no-dropdown-indicator — CONFIRMED, pre-existing, repo-wide\n\nEvery `<select>` in the radio config forms renders with `appearance: none` and\n`background-image: none`, so it has NO caret and is visually indistinguishable\nfrom a text input. Measured 2026-08-18 in Chromium at 1600x1000, both themes:\n\n  select[data-field=device_update_interval]  appearance:none  bg:none\n  select[data-field=role]                    appearance:none  bg:none\n\n  cls on both: "select select-bordered select-sm w-full"\n\nNOT INTRODUCED BY THE INTERVAL WORK. The `role` enum select has been rendered by\nthe same code path for far longer and looks identical, which is how I ruled it\nout — I checked precisely because the new interval dropdowns looked wrong and I\nwanted to know whether I had caused it.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS MORE NOW. Until today those five telemetry fields WERE text boxes,\nso looking like one was honest. They are now closed dropdowns, and the whole point\n(docs/modules/interval-options.md) is that the operator cannot type a value that\nbreaks the radio. A control that looks typeable but is not teaches the wrong\nthing, and someone will conclude the field is broken rather than that it is a\nlist.\n\nCause is almost certainly daisyUI\'s `.select` background-image being stripped —\nlikely the Tailwind CDN build or a `background-image: none` reset in\npublic/style.css. NOT investigated further; out of scope for\ninterval-tables-generated-not-transcribed, whose spec names only the generator,\nthe vendored source and interval-tables.js.\n\n  where: public/style.css + public/vendor/daisyui-4.12.14.min.css (not confirmed\n         which; the computed style is the measurement, the cause is not)\n  fix:   restore the caret for .select, then re-verify BOTH an enum field (role)\n         and a choice field (device_update_interval) in both themes'}
