2026-08-18 12:29:40,148 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'SHIPPED in 7c81c49. Spec: docs/modules/interval-tables.md.\n\n  vendor/meshtastic-android/FixedUpdateIntervals.kt   the source, verbatim\n  vendor/meshtastic-android/PROVENANCE.md             URL, upstream path, sha, date\n  scripts/gen_interval_tables.mjs                     parser; --check diffs\n  src/interval-tables.js                              GENERATED\n  src/interval-options.js                             imports it; owns only the\n                                                      field->configuration map,\n                                                      labels and decorateSchema\n  scripts/check_all.mjs                               registered as interval_tables\n\nTHE BOUNDARY, and why it is there: what upstream STATES we generate; what we INFER\nwe write and own. FIELD_CONFIGURATION is deliberately not generated — it maps our\nschema field names to the app\'s configuration names, and that correspondence\nappears nowhere in FixedUpdateIntervals.kt. It comes from the app\'s individual\nsettings screens, one DropDownPreference at a time. Generating it would mean\nparsing a dozen Compose files to recover twelve lines.\n\nVERIFICATION, all re-run at commit time:\n  - generator reproduces the file byte-for-byte; --check exits 0\n  - FALSIFIED A: change 1800 -> 1500 by hand; check names the line and exits 1\n  - FALSIFIED B: re-sort ALL (my exact original mistake); check exits 1 AND the\n    unit test fails by name on "ALL is in declaration order, NOT sorted"\n  - mechanical diff old vs generated: 16 of 17 identical, ALL the only difference,\n    same set reordered. (I had said 15 of 16 from eyeballing; there are 17\n    configurations, so 16 of 17. Substance unchanged.)\n  - npm run check: 15 of 15. check_specs: All specs current.\n\nKNOWN LIMIT, stated not hidden: nothing detects upstream moving on while the\nvendored copy sits still. The check only proves the generated file matches THIS\ncopy. Recorded in PROVENANCE.md so a green check is never read as "current with\nupstream".\n\nFOUND WHILE VERIFYING, fixed in the same commit: decorateSchema stripped min/max\nbut left `hint` and `unit`, so the new dropdowns rendered captioned "min 1800\n(firmware-enforced); 0 = use default (3600 s)" over a list that starts at 1800 and\noffers no 0. Caught by LOOKING at the browser, not by querying the DOM — the DOM\ncheck I ran first reported the select was correct, and it was; the caption beside\nit was not.\n\nFOUND, NOT FIXED (out of scope, ledger entry 82):\nselect-controls-have-no-dropdown-indicator — every <select> renders appearance:none\nwith no caret. Pre-existing; ruled out as mine by checking the `role` enum select,\nwhich is identical.'}
