2026-08-18 12:34:25,675 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'PETER, 2026-08-18, VERBATIM:\n\n"<select> in the app renders with appearance:none and no caret - may as well fix\nthat while its in memory"\n\nRaised as ledger entry 82 during interval-tables-generated-not-transcribed, where\nit was correctly ruled OUT of scope. Peter has now asked for it, so it gets its\nown task.\n\nROOT CAUSE FOUND, and it is one word.\n\ndaisyUI DOES draw the caret. From public/vendor/daisyui-4.12.14.min.css:\n\n    .select{...appearance:none;...\n      background-image:linear-gradient(45deg,transparent 50%,currentColor 50%),\n                       linear-gradient(135deg,currentColor 50%,transparent 50%);\n      background-position:calc(100% - 20px) calc(1px + 50%),\n                          calc(100% - 16.1px) calc(1px + 50%);\n      background-size:4px 4px,4px 4px;background-repeat:no-repeat}\n\nTwo little triangles forming a chevron. `appearance:none` is daisyUI\'s OWN doing\nand is correct — it removes the native arrow so daisyUI can draw its own.\n\npublic/style.css:353 then overrides it:\n\n    .input, .select, .textarea {\n      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.04) !important;\n\n`background` is the SHORTHAND. It resets every background-* longhand it does not\nmention, so background-image becomes `none`, and `!important` guarantees it beats\ndaisyUI. The caret is deleted by a rule that was only ever trying to set a tint.\n\nSo the ledger entry\'s wording was slightly wrong and is corrected here: the defect\nis NOT `appearance:none` (that is intended and must stay). It is the shorthand\nclobbering background-image.\n\nFOUR SITES, all the same mistake, found by grepping every rule whose selector\nmentions .select:\n\n  353  .input, .select, .textarea                       background: ... !important\n  361  .input:focus, .select:focus, .textarea:focus     background: ... !important\n  647  [data-theme="corporate"] .input/.select/.textarea  background: ... !important\n  652  [data-theme="corporate"] ...:focus                 background: ... !important\n\n  (368 :hover and 372 :disabled set border-color/opacity only — not implicated,\n   confirmed by reading them, not assumed from the line number.)\n\nMEASURED BEFORE THE FIX, Chromium, both themes, on TWO selects rendered by\ndifferent code paths so this is not specific to the new work:\n\n  select[data-field=device_update_interval]  (type=choice, new today)\n      appearance: none   background-image: none\n  select[data-field=role]                    (type=enum, long-standing)\n      appearance: none   background-image: none\n\nWHY IT MATTERS MORE NOW. Until today the five telemetry interval fields WERE text\nboxes, so looking like one was honest. They are now closed dropdowns, and the\nentire point (docs/modules/interval-options.md) is that an operator cannot type a\nvalue that breaks the radio. A control that looks typeable but is not teaches the\nwrong thing, and the likely conclusion is "the field is broken", not "it is a\nlist".\n\nSCOPE: public/style.css only. Browser domain, presentation only. No backend file\nis touched and no behaviour changes — this is what the control LOOKS like.'}
