2026-08-18 12:43:07,943 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'bugs', 'kind': 'note', 'text': 'slow-browser-checks-fail-with-nothing-recording-it — CONFIRMED, pre-existing\n\n`npm run check:all` is 15 of 17. The two slow browser checks BOTH fail, and unlike\nnode_api (annotated `known: \'B92, B93\'` in scripts/check_all.mjs) neither carries a\n`known:` marker, so nothing tells a reader these are expected. `npm run check` —\nthe gate people actually run — is fast+service only and never runs them, which is\nhow they can sit red unnoticed.\n\nMEASURED 2026-08-18, and proven pre-existing: with public/style.css reverted to\nHEAD the failures are byte-identical, so they are not from the select-caret fix.\n\ntests/test_page_snapshot.py — 2 failures:\n    layout: 1280x800 business    cut=1\n    layout: 1280x800 corporate   cut=1\n  One leaf element with rect.bottom > innerHeight at 1280x800, in BOTH themes.\n  1600x1000 is clean in both. Which element is not identified by the test output\n  — it reports only the count.\n\ntests/test_playwright.py — 10 failures, in three groups:\n    desktop+iphone /control tab: expected control, got overview\n    desktop+iphone /control surface Command\n    desktop+iphone /control surface Yagi Align\n      -> the Control page does not come up at all; the router lands on overview.\n         The three surface failures are almost certainly consequences of that one\n         cause, not three separate defects.\n    desktop+iphone /performance surface Traceroute History\n    iphone/messages controls in viewport: YAGI\n    alarm node has plugin section\n      sections=[\'device_vitals\',\'signal\',\'environment\',\'air_quality\',\'detections\']\n      -> expected a plugin section; got the five built-ins.\n\nNOT INVESTIGATED. Noticed while running check:all as the regression check for\nselect-caret-stripped-by-background-shorthand, and out of scope for it — that task\ntouches public/style.css only. Recorded rather than fixed, and recorded HONESTLY as\nuninvestigated: the grouping above is my reading of the output, not a traced cause.\n\nWorth its own task, and the first question is whether /control regressed or was\nnever wired — the Control page had work land on it recently (commit 1b39839\n"the Control page says when its data is stale").\n\n  next: run `python3 tests/test_playwright.py` and open /control in a browser;\n        for the layout one, have the test PRINT the offending element rather than\n        just cut=1, or it cannot be acted on without re-deriving it every time'}
2026-08-18 12:44:27,759 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'SHIPPED in 9474c81. Spec: docs/modules/select-caret.md. public/style.css only.\n\nFour rules, `background:` -> `background-color:`. The !important stays; it is still\nneeded against daisyUI\'s own background-color. `appearance: none` stays — it is\ndaisyUI\'s and it is what makes room for the drawn caret.\n\nVERIFICATION, Chromium, 1600x1000 and 1280x800, both themes:\n  17 of 17 selects carry the caret\n  0 of 76 text inputs wrongly gained one\n  0 cropped card bodies, 0 controls clipped mid-element\n  checked on BOTH render paths — role (type=enum, long-standing) and\n  device_update_interval (type=choice, new today) — so a fix reaching only the new\n  controls would have been caught\n  FALSIFIED: re-injecting the shorthand as a <style> element returns\n  backgroundImage to `none` and every caret disappears ON SCREEN; removing it\n  brings them back\n\nMETHOD NOTE WORTH KEEPING. Reading getComputedStyle immediately after setting\ndata-theme in the SAME synchronous task returns stale values — my first probe said\nboth themes were 0.024, my second said both were 0.04, and they cannot both be\nright. Set the theme in one evaluate, read in the next. I nearly reported "verified\nin both themes" off the contradictory pair.\n\nALSO CORRECTED: the theme values are `business` (dark) and `corporate` (light).\nI had been setting data-theme="dark", which matches no rule.\n\nFOUND, NOT FIXED — ledger entry 83,\nslow-browser-checks-fail-with-nothing-recording-it: `npm run check:all` is 15 of\n17. test_page_snapshot fails layout at 1280x800 in both themes (cut=1) and\ntest_playwright fails 10, most of them /control not loading at all. PROVEN\npre-existing by reverting public/style.css to HEAD and getting byte-identical\nfailures, then restoring (sha 0684184e… matches). Neither check carries a `known:`\nmarker and `npm run check` never runs them, so they sit red unnoticed.'}
