2026-08-18 12:55:52,500 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'PETER, 2026-08-18, VERBATIM:\n\n"so we are good now ?"          -> and then, on being told /control does not load:\n"yep /idiot"\n"alarm should have left node dash and should be removed"\n\nMY PREMISE WAS WRONG AND IS CORRECTED HERE. I told Peter "the Control page doesn\'t\nload ... your commit 1b39839 added staleness rendering to that page five days ago,\nand it\'s currently unreachable", which reads as a regression. It is not one. The\npage was DELETED FOUR DAYS LATER, on purpose, by him.\n\n  e8a6745  2026-08-17  feat(core): the alarm leaves node-dash — it runs as its\n                       own service on :8791\n      Peter, in that commit: "you can delete it all. I will re-add it necessary\n      in the new dash."\n      Removed 9 backend modules, public/plugins/alarm/ (6 files, 108 KB), and\n      \'/control\' from the SPA page list.\n\nAnd he has just confirmed it again: "alarm should have left node dash and should\nbe removed."\n\nVERIFIED LIVE, not inferred: http://127.0.0.1:8791/ returns 200 with\n<title>mt-alarm</title>. The Control page is alive and serving — in mt-alarm-1,\nwhere it now belongs. node-dash resolving /control to `overview` is CORRECT\nBEHAVIOUR.\n\nSo there is no app defect here. There are stale TESTS.\n\nALL 10 test_playwright failures trace to three DELIBERATE removals, all on\n2026-08-17, and not one of them is a fault in the app:\n\n  1. /control, and its "Command" and "Yagi Align" surfaces  (6 failures: desktop\n     and iphone x3). tests/test_playwright.py:67\n         RouteCase("/control", "control", ("Command","Config","Yagi Align"), "control")\n     Left with the alarm in e8a6745.\n\n  2. "alarm node has plugin section", expecting "reachability" in the node page\'s\n     sections. tests/test_playwright.py:592. The alarm plugin left in the same\n     commit, so the section it ADDED is correctly absent.\n\n  3. "Traceroute History" on /performance. tests/test_playwright.py:63.\n     Stripped 2026-08-17 in 86400ab, spec docs/modules/traceroute-removal-browser.md,\n     because the buttons were still transmitting. tab-perf.html says so at the\n     top of the file.\n\n  (the 10th, "iphone/messages controls in viewport: YAGI", is not yet traced —\n   see below, it is NOT assumed to belong to this group.)\n\nTHE TEST ALREADY CONTRADICTS ITSELF, which is the clearest evidence this is\nhalf-done maintenance rather than a discovery:\n\n    line  67  RouteCase("/control", ...)                    <- expects it to EXIST\n    line 278  "removed control tab falls back to Overview"  <- asserts it is GONE\n\nBoth in the same file, both currently asserted. One of them was updated when the\nalarm left and the other was not.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS. A check that is permanently red is not a check — it is noise that\ntrains everyone to ignore the colour. `npm run check:all` has been 15 of 17 with\nno `known:` marker on either failing check, and `npm run check` (the gate people\nactually run) never runs them, so nothing was ever going to force this.\n\nSCOPE: tests/test_playwright.py. Removing assertions about removed features.\n\nNOT IN SCOPE, and not to be quietly folded in:\n  - test_page_snapshot\'s `cut=1` layout failure at 1280x800 in both themes. That\n    check is GENERIC — it measures any element cut off — so it is not an assertion\n    about a removed feature and is probably a real layout defect. Ledger it.\n  - "iphone/messages controls in viewport: YAGI" — I have NOT traced this one.\n    It may be genuine. It must be investigated before it is touched, and it must\n    NOT be deleted just because it is adjacent to nine that are stale. Deleting a\n    real failure to make a suite green is the exact opposite of the point.'}
