2026-08-18 13:05:48,802 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'bugs', 'kind': 'note', 'text': 'messages-yagi-control-clipped-on-iphone — CONFIRMED, real, deliberately left failing\n\ntests/test_playwright.py, `iphone/messages controls in viewport: YAGI`. The check\nreports geo["clipped"], a control whose box falls outside the viewport on the\niphone profile. Generic geometry, not an assertion about any feature — which is\nexactly why it was traced individually instead of being swept up with the nine\nstale assertions removed in the same task.\n\nMEASURED 2026-08-18: it is the ONLY remaining failure in test_playwright.py, down\nfrom 10. Now annotated `known:` in scripts/check_all.mjs so the red is explained\nrather than ambient.\n\nNOT deleted, and that was the point. Nine of the ten failures were assertions about\nfeatures deliberately removed on 2026-08-17; this one is a defect. Deleting it to\nmake the suite green would have been the precise inverse of what the suite is for.\n\n  where: the messages page, YAGI control, iphone viewport only (desktop passes)\n  next:  run `python3 tests/test_playwright.py`, look at the iphone screenshot it\n         writes, and find which YAGI control overflows. Likely the radio-selector\n         row, which is a horizontal group with no wrap.\n\n---\n\npage-snapshot-layout-cut-at-1280x800 — CONFIRMED, real, uninvestigated\n\ntests/test_page_snapshot.py, `layout: 1280x800 business` and\n`layout: 1280x800 corporate`, both `cut=1`. One leaf element with\nrect.bottom > innerHeight. 1600x1000 is clean in both themes.\n\nPROVEN not from the select-caret fix: reverting public/style.css to HEAD produced\nbyte-identical failures, then restoring gave sha 0684184e… back.\n\nAlso annotated `known:` in scripts/check_all.mjs.\n\n  next:  the test prints only `cut=1` and never says WHICH element. Fix that first\n         — as it stands the offending node has to be re-derived by hand every time\n         anyone looks, which is most of why this has gone unexamined.'}
