2026-08-18 13:35:49,341 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'PETER, 2026-08-18, VERBATIM:\n\n"have you actually tried saving something and validating it was saved ? - you can\ndo that in some of the not used sections like ambient lightiung"\n\nNO, I HAD NOT. I built the whole write path today, shipped it, and never once did\na save->read-back against a real radio. Worse, I had designed the backup mechanism\nfor exactly this purpose — Peter, earlier: "it can prove that what we are writing\nto the radio is actually what the radio hold" — and never used it for it.\n\nThe very first live save found a defect. That is the whole lesson.\n\nTHE DEFECT. public/app-config.js saveSection() always posts to\n/radio-admin/config:\n\n    await fetchJSON(\'/radio-admin/config\', \'POST\',\n                    { device: target, section: sec.name, values: formValues });\n\nBut sections have a KIND. loadSections() builds them with it:\n\n    const makeSec = (name, kind) => ({ name, kind, ... });\n    ...sec.config.map(name => makeSec(name, \'config\')),\n    ...sec.module_config.map(name => makeSec(name, \'module_config\')),\n\n`kind` is written at line 109-110 and READ NOWHERE ELSE in the file. The UI even\nrenders it as a badge beside every section title, so the screen has been showing\nthe distinction the save path ignores.\n\nPROVEN LIVE, not by reading. Posting ambient_lighting the way the UI does:\n\n  POST /radio-admin/config {"section":"ambient_lighting", ...}\n  -> Bridge 500: Message type "meshtastic.protobuf.Config" has no field named\n     "ambient_lighting" at "AdminMessage.set_config".\n     Available Fields: [\'device\',\'position\',\'power\',\'network\',\'display\',\'lora\',\n                        \'bluetooth\',\'security\',\'sessionkey\',\'deviceUi\']\n\nAnd the same values via /radio-admin/module-config succeed and persist (below).\n\nBLAST RADIUS — 13 of 21 sections cannot be saved from the UI at all:\n  mqtt, serial, external_notification, store_forward, range_test, TELEMETRY,\n  canned_message, audio, remote_hardware, neighbor_info, ambient_lighting,\n  detection_sensor, paxcounter\n\nThe 8 config sections (device, position, power, network, display, lora,\nbluetooth, security) are unaffected.\n\nTELEMETRY IS IN THE BROKEN SET, which means the interval-dropdown work I shipped\nthis morning (7c81c49) saves through a path that cannot work. The feature Peter\nasked for — "send freq for metadata" — is precisely a telemetry field. I verified\nthat the CONTROL was correct and the SCHEMA was correct and never once pressed\nSave.\n\nIt fails LOUDLY rather than silently, which is the one mercy here: the operator\ngets an error, not a false success. But they get a raw protobuf error string, and\nthe save does not happen.\n\nTWO FURTHER FINDINGS FROM THE SAME EXERCISE, both recorded separately:\n\n  1. A SAVE THAT REPORTS AN ERROR MAY HAVE SUCCEEDED. My first module-config write\n     returned\n       Bridge 500: (BleakGATTProtocolErrorCode.UNLIKELY_ERROR, \'GATT Protocol\n       Error: Unlikely Error\')\n     and OMNI dropped to RECONNECTING. The write had ALREADY LANDED — after\n     reconnect and re-read, blue was 200 as sent. So a 502 from this endpoint is\n     not evidence the radio is unchanged, and any "did it save?" logic that\n     assumes otherwise is wrong.\n\n  2. FOUR UNEXPLAINED WRITES to OMNI at 11:40:32, 11:40:51, 11:49:52 and 11:56:50\n     today. A backup exists only because write() ran, and write() is only reached\n     from the six setters. Neither test reproduces it now (ran both, backup count\n     unchanged), and an idle browser on /devices for 60s does not either. The\n     backups are IDENTICAL once `ts` is excluded, so nothing actually changed on\n     the radio — but four writes were issued and I cannot say by what.\n\nWHAT DID WORK, and it is worth stating because it is the part I could not have\nclaimed before: the module-config round trip is genuinely proven.\n     146 -> 200  written, survived a BLE reconnect, read back 200\n     200 -> 146  written, survived a BLE reconnect, read back 146\nSurviving a reconnect-and-resync is the strongest available confirmation: the\nvalue is in the radio\'s flash, not in anyone\'s cache. current/red/green were\npreserved throughout, so sending the full section is correct and nothing was\nzeroed.\n\nSCOPE: public/app-config.js saveSection. One branch on sec.kind.'}
