2026-08-18 13:44:03,821 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'SHIPPED in 286e70d. Spec: docs/modules/app-config.md, section "A section\'s KIND\ndecides which admin field it is saved to — 2026-08-18".\n\nONE LINE in public/app-config.js saveSection():\n\n    const path = sec.kind === \'module_config\' ? \'module-config\' : \'config\';\n    await fetchJSON(`/radio-admin/${path}`, \'POST\', {...});\n\nThe backend already had both endpoints and both verbs. Only the browser\'s choice\nbetween them was missing. Unknown kind falls back to \'config\' on purpose — `kind`\ncomes from the backend\'s own /sections, so a third value means that contract\nchanged, and keeping the 8 working sections working beats breaking all 21.\n\nVERIFIED THROUGH THE REAL UI, not curl. Clicked OMNI > Radio > ambient lighting,\ntyped into the field, pressed Save:\n\n  146 -> 199   POST /radio-admin/module-config => 200; radio reads back 199\n  FALSIFIED    forced path back to \'config\' -> POST /radio-admin/config => 502\n               Bad Gateway, console error, save fails. Restored -> 200 again.\n  199 -> 146   restored; radio reads back 146\n\nEvery read-back was taken after OMNI reconnected and re-synced, so the value is in\nthe radio\'s flash and not in anyone\'s cache. That is the strongest confirmation\navailable without a serial console.\n\nnpm run check 15/15, check_specs "All specs current."\n\nINCIDENTAL CONFIRMATION, worth keeping. Each successful module-config write\ndropped OMNI to RECONNECTING and it came back holding the new value — three times,\nconsistently. We send no reboot command and none of the edit-transaction verbs, so\nthis is the firmware restarting itself. Peter, 2026-08-17: "the device will\nrestart itself if it needs to and that may NOT be a manual request." Directly\nobserved, and it retrospectively justifies the decision not to send reboot_seconds.\n\nTHE LESSON, which is bigger than the fix. I verified the control and I verified\nthe schema and I never pressed Save. Every check I wrote for the interval work\npassed — unit tests, a served-schema assertion, a browser render at two sizes in\ntwo themes — and none of them touched the one path that mattered. A save button is\nnot verified by anything except saving.\n\nFOUND, NOT FIXED — ledger entries 85:\n  radio-backup-omits-every-module-config-section  <- taking this next\n  save-error-does-not-mean-the-write-failed\n  four-unexplained-writes-to-omni (cause UNKNOWN; tests measured and ruled out)'}
