2026-08-18 14:31:04,067 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'bugs', 'kind': 'note', 'text': 'RETRACTION — radio-backup-omits-every-module-config-section IS FALSE\n\nI raised that entry today, put it in commit 286e70d\'s message, and told Peter twice.\nIt is wrong and is withdrawn.\n\nmesh-gw\'s /radio_backup returns THREE top-level keys — config, module_config,\nchannels — and the saved files contain all three. Measured on\nbackups/!2687afb1/260818134042.json:\n\n    top-level keys: version, node_id, ts, config, module_config, channels\n    module sections present: 15   (incl. telemetry, ambient_lighting, mqtt,\n                                   and even tak + traffic_management, which are\n                                   not in /sections)\n    channels present: 8\n\nHOW I GOT IT WRONG. I inspected doc[\'config\'] only, found no telemetry /\nambient_lighting / mqtt in it, and reported them missing FROM THE FILE. They were\none level across, in doc[\'module_config\'].\n\nThat is exactly the failure CLAUDE.md names: "An absence is a claim, and claims get\nchecked... Enumerate the tables, read the schema, open the module." I declared an\nabsence without enumerating the container. The rule exists because a false absence\nproduces work built on a wrong premise — here it nearly produced a "fix" to a\nmechanism that was already correct.\n\nTHE BACKUP IS VERIFIED, properly this time, across all 21 sections rather than a\n6-section sample:\n\n    sections compared: 21   MATCH: 20   differ: 1\n    ambient_lighting  backup={"blue":199,...}  live={"blue":146,...}\n\nThe one difference is the mechanism WORKING: that file was written immediately\nbefore the save that set blue back to 146, so it holds the pre-save state. Across\nfour consecutive saves the chain reads 200 -> 146 -> 199 -> 199, each the value as\nit stood before that write.\n\n(Comparison must strip keys beginning `__`: /config/{section} adds __reboot and\n__notes for the form, radio_backup carries neither. Not stripping them reports 8\nspurious mismatches — my first pass did exactly that and I nearly filed THAT as a\nfinding too.)\n\n---\n\nbackup-files-are-world-writable-and-hold-a-private-key — CONFIRMED, needs Peter\n\nThe backup files contain real secrets and are readable and WRITABLE by anyone:\n\n    drwxrwsrwx  backups/\n    drwxrwsrwx  backups/!2687afb1/\n    -rw-rw-rw-  backups/!2687afb1/260818134042.json\n\n    security.private_key : PRESENT\n    channel psks         : 2  (incl. the Private channel)\n    mqtt.password        : PRESENT, plaintext\n    sessionkey           : {}   <- correctly EMPTY, no passkey stored\n\nWORLD-WRITABLE IS THE WORSE HALF. The whole value of this directory is that it is\nan audit chain — "a full record of all changes made to any device". A record any\nprocess can rewrite is not a record.\n\nNOT INTRODUCED BY US, and this is why it is Peter\'s call rather than a fix I should\njust make: the entire repo tree is drwxrwsrwx — `.`, src, public and data all carry\nit — and src/radio-admin.js passes no mode to mkdirSync or writeFileSync, so the\nfiles inherit the environment. umask is 0022, so the mode is coming from the tree,\nnot the process.\n\nCorrectly gitignored (.gitignore:10), so none of it is committed.\n\n  options, for Peter:\n    a) leave it — the tree is deliberately permissive and this box is trusted\n    b) have radio-admin write these files 0600 explicitly, since they are the only\n       files in the repo containing a device private key\n    c) tighten the tree, which is outside node-dash\'s remit\n  I have NOT changed any permission. Doing so unasked could break whatever\n  needs the tree open.'}
2026-08-18 14:34:04,596 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'SHIPPED in a1f7636. Spec: docs/modules/radio-admin.md, section "Two comments in\nthis module were false — 2026-08-18".\n\nsrc/radio-admin.js — comments only, no behaviour change:\n  - the begin/commit claim corrected: single save = bare set, bulk profile install\n    = editSettings transaction. The rule is about COUNT, not principle, and the\n    next person adding restore-a-whole-config needs the transaction.\n  - the "6 of 6 sections" note replaced with a real 21-section verification, plus\n    the coverage facts (3 top-level keys, 15 module sections, 8 channels,\n    sessionkey empty) and the `__`-stripping trap.\n\nVERIFIED:\n  - grep of the vendored app source: begin_edit_settings at AdminControllerImpl\n    :371, commit at :382, editSettings called from InstallProfileUseCase:85, and\n    RadioConfigUseCase:95/:125 calling radioController.setConfig/setModuleConfig\n    with no transaction. Both halves of the corrected claim shown from source.\n  - backup vs live across all 21 sections: MATCH 20, differ 1, the difference\n    being the intended pre-save record.\n  - tests/test_radio_admin.mjs 14 checks pass — including its assertion that we\n    still send NO transaction, which the correction does not disturb.\n  - FALSIFIED by reproducing my own error: reading doc[\'config\'] alone returns\n    None for telemetry/ambient_lighting/mqtt and yields the false conclusion;\n    enumerating the container first shows 15 module sections and 8 channels.\n  - npm run check 15/15, All specs current.\n\nHONEST NOTE ON THE RUN: an intermediate `npm run check` gave 13/15 with\ncheck_snapshot and node_api failing. That was MY doing — those read live counts and\nOMNI was rebooting from the ambient_lighting saves I had just made. check_snapshot\nalone: 54 checks, 0 mismatches; the re-run is clean. Recorded rather than quietly\nre-run until green.\n\nTHE REAL OUTPUT OF THIS TASK IS A RETRACTION. I published "the backup omits every\nmodule_config section" in a ledger entry, in commit 286e70d\'s message, and to Peter\ntwice. It is false, and the method that produced it — inspecting one key of a\ndocument and reporting what was not in it as missing from the file — is the exact\nfailure CLAUDE.md legislates against. Twice more in the same hour I nearly repeated\nit: the 8 spurious mismatches from not stripping `__`, and a first reading of the\npermissions before checking sibling directories.\n\nFOUND, NOT FIXED — ledger entry 86:\n  backup-files-are-world-writable-and-hold-a-private-key. security.private_key, 2\n  channel PSKs and the MQTT password in plaintext at -rw-rw-rw-. NOT ours: the\n  whole tree is drwxrwsrwx and this code passes no mode. Peter\'s call; no\n  permission changed.'}
