2026-08-18 14:34:50,709 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'PETER, 2026-08-18, VERBATIM, stated as permanent:\n\n"how does phone app handle it. that will always be my reply"\n\nApplied to my OWN comments in src/radio-admin.js, it found two claims that do not\nsurvive the question, and one published finding that is outright false.\n\nCLAIM 1, FALSE. The file said the app "does NOT use begin/commit edit settings\nanywhere". AdminControllerImpl.editSettings does exactly that — begin_edit_settings\nat :371, commit_edit_settings at :382, awaiting acceptance of both boundaries.\n\nThe conclusion it was defending still holds, but for a narrower reason:\n    single-section save  -> bare setConfig/setModuleConfig, NO transaction\n                            (RadioConfigUseCase:95/:125)\n    bulk profile install -> editSettings { ... }  (InstallProfileUseCase:85)\n                            begin, every section, commit — 13+ reboots into one\nSo the rule is about COUNT, not principle. "Anywhere" would mislead whoever adds\nrestore-a-whole-config, which is precisely when the transaction is required.\n\nCLAIM 2, TRUE BUT MISLEADING. "Verified 2026-08-18 against genuine radio reads:\nmatched on 6 of 6 sections". Six of twenty-one is a sample worded as a\nverification. Redone across all 21: MATCH 20, differ 1, and the one difference is\nambient_lighting holding the value from before the save that file precedes — the\nmechanism working.\n\nCLAIM 3, RETRACTED ENTIRELY. Earlier today I reported "the backup omits every\nmodule_config section — all 13 absent", filed it in the ledger, wrote it into\ncommit 286e70d, and told Peter twice.\n\nIt is false. radio_backup returns THREE top-level keys — config, module_config,\nchannels — and the saved files carry all three: 15 module sections and 8 channels.\nI had read doc[\'config\'] only, found no telemetry in it, and reported it missing\nfrom the FILE. It was one level across.\n\nThat is the exact failure CLAUDE.md legislates against: "An absence is a claim, and\nclaims get checked... Enumerate the tables, read the schema, open the module." I\ndeclared an absence without enumerating the container, and it nearly produced a\n"fix" to a mechanism that was already correct.\n\nSCOPE: src/radio-admin.js comments and its spec. No behaviour change — the code\nthis describes is right; only the description was wrong.'}
