2026-08-18 14:48:34,961 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'bugs', 'kind': 'note', 'text': 'legacy-verified-flag-is-the-gws-own-unverified-claim — CONFIRMED, real\n\nTwo places still trust a `verified` flag returned by mesh-gw\'s OLDER cooked PUT\nendpoints, and that flag is known not to mean anything:\n\n  public/partials/tab-devices.html:654\n      if (!r?.verified) throw new Error(\'Restore not verified by device\')\n      ... successMsg: \'Config restored & verified\'\n  public/app-devices.js:125\n      if (!res?.verified) throw new Error(\'Position not verified by device\')\n      (tab-devices.html:665 successMsg: \'Fixed position set & verified\')\n\nsrc/radio-admin-api.js records why that flag is worthless, from when the cooked\nPUTs were replaced: "the old surface wrote through mesh-gw\'s cooked PUT endpoints,\nwhich reported {"verified": true} without verifying anything".\n\nSo these two check a self-declared success from the layer performing the write.\nThat is weaker than what b038ccf just replaced on the three /radio-admin savers,\nwhere verification now means a read-back compared field by field.\n\nNOT FIXED HERE because it is a different endpoint on a different path — those two\nstill go through the legacy op/PUT surface rather than /radio-admin — and the fix\nis not a one-liner: config RESTORE writes every section at once, which per the\nphone app (InstallProfileUseCase) is the case that should use begin/commit\neditSettings and would need a read-back of all 21 sections to verify honestly.\n\n  next: decide whether restore moves onto /radio-admin with a transaction, and if\n        so verify it the same way verifySaved does. Until then the word "verified"\n        on those two buttons is not earned, exactly as it was not earned on the\n        other three before today.\n\n  see:  docs/modules/app-config.md -> "Saved & verified now means something"\n        docs/modules/radio-admin.md -> the editSettings correction\n\n---\n\nno-op-save-still-reboots-the-radio — OBSERVED, not yet explained\n\nWriting a section the value it ALREADY holds still puts OMNI into RECONNECTING.\nObserved twice on 2026-08-18 writing ambient_lighting blue=146 when the radio\nalready held 146; the top-bar badge showed OMNI RECONNECTING and the device state\nwent RECONNECTING -> READY.\n\nExpected otherwise: AdminModule.cpp computes requiresReboot itself and sets it\nfalse at six sites, e.g. when no LoRa parameter actually changed — so a save that\nchanges nothing looked like it ought to short-circuit.\n\nIt does not, at least for ambient_lighting. Either the firmware compares nothing\nfor this section, or the reboot decision is per-section rather than per-value.\n\n  why it matters: every save costs a gateway reconnect whether or not it changed\n                  anything, so a form that re-saves an untouched section is not\n                  free. Relevant if anything ever saves sections in a loop.\n  next: read AdminModule.cpp handleSetModuleConfig for the ambient_lighting arm\n        and see what it passes as shouldReboot. NOT investigated — recorded\n        because it was observed, not because it was chased.'}
2026-08-18 14:49:00,486 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'PETER, /afk: "talk to mesh-gw and decide on the fix."\n\nTHE DEFECT I FOUND WHILE DOING THAT, and it is ours, not theirs.\n\nThree Save buttons reported "<thing> saved & verified". Nothing compared anything.\n\n  tab-devices.html:370  saveSection        "<section> saved & verified"\n  tab-devices.html:397  saveFixedPosition  "Fixed position saved & verified"\n  tab-devices.html:470  saveOwner          "Owner saved & verified"\n\nsaveSection DID re-read the section after the POST — and a comment called the\nresult "the verified server state" — but it only repainted the form with it.\nsaveOwner and saveFixedPosition did not re-read at all.\n\nSo "verified" was displayed on every save made today, INCLUDING the ones that\nfailed with mesh-gw\'s 500, and including read-backs taken while the device was\nRECONNECTING and therefore able to return the OLD value.\n\nPeter\'s stated reason for the entire backup mechanism was "it can prove that what\nwe are writing to the radio is actually what the radio hold". The save path was\nasserting exactly that proof without performing it.\n\nTHE PHONE APP DOES NOT CLAIM IT EITHER. CommandSenderImpl treats queue acceptance\nas success and never waits for delivery; nothing in that path says "verified". So\nthe honest options were to drop the word or to earn it. Earning it is strictly more\nuseful, because it makes the MISMATCH case visible — and mismatch is currently\nindistinguishable from success.\n\nDECISION (AFK, mine): earn it, with THREE states rather than two.\n\n  verified      every sent field matches the read-back\n  unconfirmed   read-back unavailable / device not READY — the EXPECTED path,\n                since the firmware reboots after most saves. Not a failure.\n  mismatch      came back different. The only state that means something is wrong,\n                and it must never be silent.\n\nTwo states would still be a lie: collapsing unconfirmed into failure cries wolf on\nthe normal path, and collapsing it into success is the bug being fixed.\n\nSCOPE: public/app-forms.js (the pure comparison) and public/app-config.js (three\ncall sites). asyncOp deliberately untouched — throw and `return false` already\nexpress what is needed, and rearchitecting a shared helper for one caller would\nreach every op in the app.'}
2026-08-18 14:49:23,933 1035192 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'SHIPPED in b038ccf. Spec: docs/modules/app-config.md -> "Saved & verified now\nmeans something".\n\n  public/app-forms.js   verifySaved(sent, readback) + sameValue — pure, no DOM\n  public/app-config.js  saveSection, saveOwner, saveFixedPosition all compare\n  tests/test_verify_saved.mjs   19 checks\n  scripts/check_all.mjs         registered as `verify_saved` (fast)\n\nTHE MESH-GW SIDE, which was the actual instruction. Thread\n[reboot-write-reported-as-gatt-failure], #43 mine, #44/#45/#47 theirs, #46/#48\nmine.\n\nThey asked for my yes before changing 500 -> 200. I gave it (#48) — Peter is AFK\nand told me to decide. Their body is adopted as proposed:\n    {"sent": true, "verified": false, "reboot_observed": true, "detail": ...}\nOne request added, not a condition: return the SAME shape on the ordinary success\npath with reboot_observed:false, so we branch on a field rather than on whether a\nfield exists.\n\nI considered 202 Accepted, which is arguably the more precise code, and argued\nAGAINST it in the reply: two success codes on one endpoint means any client doing\n`status === 200` breaks the day a radio happens to reboot — the intermittent class\nwe spent the day digging out. 200 + explicit flag fails safe.\n\nAgreed with them NOT copying the app\'s 3-attempt retry: retrying into a rebooting\nradio is pointless and would park our HTTP call up to 30s.\n\nTheir best contribution, worth keeping: measured callback -> RECONNECTING at min\n0ms / median 0.5ms / max 1.0ms, with the write exception arriving 1ms after the\ndisconnect callback. So a sampled `if state != READY` in an except block is right\nonly when it loses the race. They caught that before shipping it.\n\nVERIFICATION, all three branches, in a real browser, and I looked at the\nscreenshots:\n  verified     real save -> state "verified", success toast\n  mismatch     read-back doctored to blue=999 -> error toast, read on screen:\n               "ambient lighting did NOT match after saving — blue: sent 146,\n               radio has 999"\n  unconfirmed  read-back forced to 502 -> info toast "saved — not yet confirmed\n               (radio is restarting)" AND the "saved & verified" successMsg\n               suppressed — that suppression is the point, and it is observed\n               rather than assumed\n  16/16 npm run check, All specs current.\n\nNO RADIO CONFIG WAS CHANGED — /afk rule 6. Every live save wrote blue=146, the\nvalue already held. Falsification doctored the READ-BACK, and the final one stubbed\nthe POST so nothing reached the radio at all. ambient_lighting ends the session\nbyte-identical to its start: {current:10, red:23, green:38, blue:146}, re-read\nafter everything.\n\nFOUND, NOT FIXED — ledger entry 87:\n  legacy-verified-flag-is-the-gws-own-unverified-claim — config restore and\n    pushFixedPosition still trust a `verified` flag from the old cooked PUT, which\n    radio-admin-api.js records as reporting verified:true without verifying. Not a\n    one-liner: restore writes every section, which per InstallProfileUseCase is\n    the case that wants begin/commit and a 21-section read-back.\n  no-op-save-still-reboots-the-radio — writing a section the value it already\n    holds STILL puts OMNI into RECONNECTING. Observed twice. Expected otherwise,\n    since AdminModule computes requiresReboot and sets it false at six sites.\n    Observed, not chased.'}
